{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons","id":85157,"title":"Kill Six Billion Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-06T00:22:56-08:00","id":85157,"title":"Kill Six Billion Demons","content":"Okay so the friggin wonderful piece of art known as Kill Six Billion Demons is a relatively new webcomic but why haven't I heard about it till now? I'm glad Solar posted it on the Exalted Media thread but honestly this needs its own thread! I just read all of it so far and its friggin outstanding! Its very rare to have something of this caliber in either writing or visual depictions but to have them both together?! <br /> <br /> I recommend when you read it you read the message in the comment section of almost each new page from the creator as a brief piece of art or a wonderful piece of writing follows, often in response to comments from previous pages.<br /> <br /> Seriously this is brilliant, one of the best comics if not stories I've seen. Its a great example of the out there cool fiction outside the default western approach, and a good inspiration for exalted if you want more exotic style beyond the Chinese and Japanese motiffs. Its a satisfying blend of gnostic, hindu, and comic book sci fi! And one of the main characters is a Kung Fu Angel Monk! Its honestly great primordial inspiration that can be applied to Yu-Shan or Malfeas!<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/?comic=ksbd-3-42#comment-3768\" target=\"_blank\">http://killsixbilliondemons.com/?comic=ksbd-3-42#comment-3768<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/ksbd42.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T00:27:54-08:00","id":85158,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> <b>Liturgy</b><br /><br /> </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">PSALMS</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">BOOK I</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2013</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\"> I. ROYALTY</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">-YS ATUN VRAMA PRESH-</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">-THE SEVEN SYLLABLES OF ROYALTY-</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">1. YISUN said: let there not be a genesis, for beginnings are false and I am a consummate liar.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">2. The full of it is this \u2013 the circular suicide of God is is the perfection of matter.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">3. YISUN lied once and said he had nine hundred and ninety nine thousand names. This is true, but it is also a barefaced lie. The true name of God is I.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">4. Living is an exercise of violence. Exercise of violence is the fate of living</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">5. Violence is circular. Perception is not circular and lacks flawlessness- therefore, rejoice in imperfect things, for their rareness is not lacking!</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">6. Love of self is the true exercise of the God called I.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">7. Only an idiot cannot place his absolute certainty in paradoxes. The divine suicide is a perfect paradox. A man cannot exist without paradox \u2013 that is the full of it.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">II.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">THE KING IN THE TOWER</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">1. YISUN is the supreme king.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">2. YISUN has, had, and will have no equal or rival save YISUN, for none may surpass YISUN in the perfect art of continual self annihilation.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">3. YISUN was the untouchable and prime master of all seven syllables of royalty but only knew four exquisite ways of lying. The first four are:</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">i. Lying of substance \u2013 the illusion of corporeality</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">ii. Lying of emptiness \u2013 the illusion of differential space</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">iii. Lying of the Ego \u2013 the illusion of self and conscious mind</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">iv. Lying of Continuity of Existence \u2013 the illusion of singularity</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">III.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">THE GRAND ENEMY CALLED I</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">YISUN sat once with his disciple Hansa in YISUN\u2019s second clockwise glass palace. Hansa was one of his most ardent students and a grand questioner of YISUN. Unlike Yisun\u2019s other disciple, Pree Ashma, he had no hunger in his heart for dominion of the universe, but a miserly scrutiny and a heart of iron nails. He was not an aspirant for royalty, and thereby attained it through little effort.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">Hansa\u2019s questions were thus:</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018Lord, how must I question space?\u2019</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018With an age, an ant may encircle a giant five million times,\u2019 spoke YISUN.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018Lord, how then may I question time?\u2019</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018A giant\u2019s stride takes an ant a week to surpass.\u2019 YISUN spoke and smiled in the 4th way.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">Hansa was discontent with this answer and rubbed the stem of his long and worn pipe which he always kept with him and would eventually lead to his annihilation. Since he was royalty, he knew this, and kept it close to him as a reminder of his circular death.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018Lord, then which should I be, the giant or the ant?\u2019</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2018Both,\u2019 spoke YISUN,\u2019 or either, when it suits you. Destroy the grand enemy called \u2018I\u2019.\u2019</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">Hansa contemplated this in silence. Later he would recount this proverb to his daughter.</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#EA2F45\">\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2013</span></div> </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.thecomicage.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Kill6BillionDemons006-1024x664.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.thecomicage.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Kill6BillionDemons005-791x1024.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.thecomicage.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/Kill6BillionDemons004-794x1024.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T07:19:25-08:00","id":85291,"title":"","content":"I got put on to it by Minton. It's good stuff!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T08:11:34-08:00","id":85337,"title":"","content":"Yeah, even though it focuses entirely on esoteric otherworldly stuff I think this is probably the most Exalted-y webcomic, <i>possibly </i>including the actual Exalted webcomics. The text segments at the bottom remind me a lot of Dunsany. At the very least, it's an invaluable Malfeas inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T09:40:47-08:00","id":85412,"title":"","content":"This is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T10:31:13-08:00","id":85441,"title":"","content":"Saw it last night on the Exalted Media thread, just finished catching up a minute ago. Talk about top-notch Exalted brain fodder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T11:17:28-08:00","id":85475,"title":"","content":"Woah. That's pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T12:12:37-08:00","id":85516,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this comic is pretty much what Malfeas looks like, in my games.<br /> <br /> Also? If anyone who makes Exalted development decisions is reading this thread? We should definitely commission this artist for some Malfeas art at some point in the line. Just sayin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:23:04-08:00","id":85629,"title":"","content":"The style reminds me vaguely of Guy Davis'. It might be the rough but expansive details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 03-06-2014, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T14:39:23-08:00","id":85643,"title":"","content":"I ran into this a while ago. It's like Dunsany writing Planescape. <br /> <br /> Honestly it's so good it makes me feel bad that I will never make anything even close.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T16:01:36-08:00","id":85696,"title":"","content":"Yeah Kill Six Billion Demons is totally immense and really, I should have posted it up earlier. As soon as I found it I thought &quot;holy fuck, so Exalted&quot; (also Mage?) but never got around to showing it off a bit until the media thread kicked off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T16:26:03-08:00","id":85709,"title":"","content":"Yeah it does give inspiration for the Supernal the denizens and intriguing methods to use gnosticism in stories. Supernal Truth portrayed in scenes, parables, psalms and the like. Makes me think Buddhist Jataka stories are examples the supernal and past versions of reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> But this is a very excellent method for including the Shinma in game. I can now see Deva/God/Raksha religions and cults following Shinma, and I finally see the Shinma anthropomorphized in the psalms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T16:27:38-08:00","id":85710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=85516#post85516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this comic is pretty much what Malfeas looks like, in my games.<br /> <br /> Also? If anyone who makes Exalted development decisions is reading this thread? We should definitely commission this artist for some Malfeas art at some point in the line. Just sayin'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I was thinking this! It would be pretty cool to get some Cameo art commissioned like how Adam Warren did the Glorious Divininity covers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T16:37:10-08:00","id":85712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=85337#post85337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, even though it focuses entirely on esoteric otherworldly stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>I like esoteric otherworldly stuff as it relates to Exalted because it gives a good reference point for what the arcane secrets to be found plumbing the depths of Malfeas or its glass libraries, or the tombs of the Neverborn, or the shifting currents of the Wyld actually <i>are</i>, and from there you can branch off into thinking of what kinds of cool shit to make out of them.<br /> <br /> I once thought of the idea of an Exalt investigating the strange etiquette and protocol of Yozi communication amongst and within themselves, which could be used as the basis for a complex information retention and transmission system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:51:10-08:00","id":86289,"title":"","content":"The original MSPA CYOA thread","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T05:30:18-08:00","id":86690,"title":"","content":"Well Damn. This is awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/950-finaliteration","name":"Finaliteration","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T09:54:58-08:00","id":86826,"title":"","content":"Great art, but the writing - especially the below-comic extras - seems like the religious/spiritual bits are tacked on. In particular, many of the flourishes seem to advertise &quot;this is from the age when people didn't know how to tell stories that well&quot; rather than &quot;this is mystical&quot;.<br /> <br /> One illustrative example is when the peace keeper speaks of knowing &quot;of&quot; the fourth syllable: that literally just means it knows that there are at least four syllables. If it meant that it knew the fourth syllable, then it should have said so; if it meant to state some sort of half-knowledge, then it should have said that. Saying that it knows &quot;of&quot; the fourth syllable as if that is meaningful implies, among other things, not immediately knowing &quot;of&quot; the first, second, and third syllables - i.e., that this character is incapable of basic logical deduction, which is a mental limitation inconsistent with the rest of the character's portrayal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T10:24:13-08:00","id":86845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winged Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=86826#post86826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One illustrative example is when the peace keeper speaks of knowing &quot;of&quot; the fourth syllable: that literally just means it knows that there are at least four syllables. If it meant that it knew the fourth syllable, then it should have said so; if it meant to state some sort of half-knowledge, then it should have said that. Saying that it knows &quot;of&quot; the fourth syllable as if that is meaningful implies, among other things, not immediately knowing &quot;of&quot; the first, second, and third syllables - i.e., that this character is incapable of basic logical deduction, which is a mental limitation inconsistent with the rest of the character's portrayal.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;have knowledge of&quot; is a fairly well established (if baroque) way of saying &quot;comprehend/know&quot;. See, e.g. Proverbs 30: 3 &quot;I have not learned wisdom, nor have I knowledge of the Holy One.&quot;<br /> <br /> The writer is not saying &quot;I don't know that the Holy One exists&quot; he's saying &quot;I don't know *who/what&quot; the Holy One is&quot;.<br /> <br /> Likewise, &quot;having knowledge of the fourth syllable&quot; does in fact mean &quot;knowing what the fourth syllable is&quot; not just &quot;knowing that there are at least four syllables&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's an appropriate phrasing giving that it's supposed to be from a religious text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/782-lafing-cat","name":"Lafing Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T10:38:02-08:00","id":86850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Winged Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=86826#post86826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;this is from the age when people didn't know how to tell stories that well&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultural bias.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T10:55:57-08:00","id":86863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>doran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=86289#post86289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original MSPA CYOA thread</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Didn't MSPA itself originally launch as a weird thread in the Penny Arcade forums? Following that pedigree, I'm interested in seeing what happens when it reaches the &quot;legions of hardcore cosplay fans&quot; stage of development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",