d":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:58:28-07:00","id":512960,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bah. This multiverse is broken. Time to throw it out and buy a new one.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:05:01-07:00","id":513346,"title":"","content":"I can't remember, in that origin story, was it the Servants who came first? Meaning that 82's reference to the second born is a poetic way of stating that Michael is the very first angel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:20:50-07:00","id":513356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=513346#post513346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember, in that origin story, was it the Servants who came first? Meaning that 82's reference to the second born is a poetic way of stating that Michael is the very first angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/ksbd-5-86/\" target=\"_blank\">Link to the story in question.</a><br /> <br /> Koss made the Servants first who,being living beings with their own Will eventually rebelled in some fashion. To fix this, he made the Angels(also called Aeons) and infused them with Law so that they would go out and bring order and hopefully also not rebel.<br /> <br /> Then Ashma was.......herself. And Humans happened.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:40:44-07:00","id":513575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=513346#post513346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember, in that origin story, was it the Servants who came first? Meaning that 82's reference to the second born is a poetic way of stating that Michael is the very first angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be.<br /> I wondered if he might have been the first of the smaller Humanoid Angels. You know, as opposed to the giant Primes that King Zoss killed.<br /> Hmm-... Maybe there's still a living giant Prime out there? Michael is after all '2', not '1'.<br /> <br /> I still wonder how the Angelic numbering system works. The story of Koss seems to hint that there are 777 of them, which means 82 and 23 must be quite high up in there hierarchy-... Assuming numbers and ranks are entirely dependent on age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:15:40-07:00","id":513666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=513575#post513575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could be.<br /> I wondered if he might have been the first of the smaller Humanoid Angels. You know, as opposed to the giant Primes that King Zoss killed.<br /> Hmm-... Maybe there's still a living giant Prime out there? Michael is after all '2', not '1'.<br /> <br /> I still wonder how the Angelic numbering system works. The story of Koss seems to hint that there are 777 of them, which means 82 and 23 must be quite high up in there hierarchy-... Assuming numbers and ranks are entirely dependent on age.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> With 2 Michael and <a href=\"http://orbitaldropkick.tumblr.com/post/82091686323/the-angel-called-6-juggernaut-star-scours-the\" target=\"_blank\">6 Juggernaut Star Scours the Universe</a> both in high ranking positions, my initial reaction is to assume that the number at the start of their name corresponds to their rank or power.<br /> <br /> 23, however, complicates things because 82 had no particular reaction to her other than &quot;Oh shit, another Angel trying to stab my face out&quot; and they seemed fairly equal in combat ability when they fought.<br /> <br /> Then I considered that the Number may relate to age of the angel, but again, 23 makes that complicated. <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/kill-six-billion-demons-chapter-4/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> among the other people getting pointed out, 23 is called a Vapor Angel and 82, a Liquid Angel. Over <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/ksbd-4-57/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, Liquid and Vapor Angels are referred to as &quot;young Angels.&quot;<br /> <br /> Presumably, there's another &quot;state&quot; of Angel. Traditionally, it would be Solid and I would be inclined to those are the oldest among the angels. That would <i>probably</i> mean the order goes Vapor to Liquid to Solid Angels, which would mean that 23 is the younger between her and 82. However, then I remembered that Angels are controlled nuclear explosions, so the order may instead go Liquid to Vapor to Plasma, meaning that it would be 82 that's the younger one and would seem to match the convention of lower number angels being older.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not particularly sure. 23 didn't really strike me as particularly old. Or rather, as I am certain that 23 is ancient by mortal standards, she didn't strike me as particularly old relative to Angels, nor did her actions towards 82 particularly strike me as those of an elder to their younger, but more of relative peers on opposite sides.<br /> <br /> So, like the rest of this comic, plenty of speculation and waiting with baited breath for answers, very little in the way of anything concrete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T02:26:08-07:00","id":513979,"title":"","content":"Maybe 23 and 82 are old by the order of their creation by Koss, but are young in the sense that they have recently been reincarnated?<br /> <br /> Hmm-... I wonder if Prime has a place in the Angelic State Cycle. Perhaps it goes from Liquid, to Vapour, to Plasma, to Prime? Bah, we probably won't be able to find a satisfying answer until we have much more information.<br /> But it is such fun to speculate, I find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T03:31:39-07:00","id":514005,"title":"","content":"Is humanity /just/ homo sapiens, or would what we call aliens also be humanity by having the same type of souls and mortality? That is, is Incubus, Jadis and Mammon currently the only human demiurges with the others being of the Servant types?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T04:19:00-07:00","id":514012,"title":"","content":"Are you mixing up Mammon and Mottom?<br /> <br /> Which would be understandable, Lord knows I've done it enough.<br /> <br /> I also think Solomon looks fairly human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:02:35-07:00","id":514039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>doran</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=514005#post514005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is humanity /just/ homo sapiens, or would what we call aliens also be humanity by having the same type of souls and mortality? That is, is Incubus, Jadis and Mammon currently the only human demiurges with the others being of the Servant types?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was wondering that very thing myself.<br /> I'm also thinking that Jagganoth might actually be a Devil, and if his weird head thing is actually his mask. And Gog-Agog might be something weirder still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:51:16-07:00","id":514183,"title":"","content":"The artwork of the ancient demi-urges shows some figures that aren't humanoid. But the recent pages say humans are the only true mortals. So I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:55:01-07:00","id":514187,"title":"","content":"The demi-urges could be transcendent Humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:42:11-07:00","id":514309,"title":"","content":"Or being a Demiurge can be something totally independent of whether or not you start as a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/avatars/3507685/Exalted_Back.small.jpg?1370109312\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/446-nervaqus987","name":"Nervaqus987","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar446_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T16:56:52-07:00","id":514621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nervaqus987</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=514309#post514309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or being a Demiurge can be something totally independent of whether or not you start as a human.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would appear to be the case, considering Mammon.<br /> I also recall seeing on page 3-44 that there was Demiurge who looked like Omun Vash, which originally lead me to believe they were a weird race of Perceivers rather than Sustainers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T17:40:01-07:00","id":514668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=513979#post513979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe 23 and 82 are old by the order of their creation by Koss, but are young in the sense that they have recently been reincarnated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being capable of reincarnation, maybe the number indicates the number of lives they've gone through? Being first of the secondborn doesn't seem as big a deal unless he can still be counted among the secondborn (hence 2). 23 Might not be significantly older because she has only reincarnated recently. Lower numbers might indicate power by virtue that fewer lives may mean they've lived longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/214-brontes","name":"Brontes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:36:35-07:00","id":521790,"title":"","content":"New <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-1-4/\" target=\"_blank\">Page</a> up.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> Man, that is the first age in a nut shell. One of my favorite pages thus far.<br /> <br /> Also, the classic lament of angels: Free Will Ruins Everything.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 05-20-2015, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T06:39:22-07:00","id":521793,"title":"","content":"I think this is my favourite page yet.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I particularly like all of the subtle (and occasionally less subtle, but still fun) ways it represents the vices of the Seven.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> We've got:<br /> Mammon off on his own, staring enraptured at a pile of streaming coins.<br /> <br /> Incubus playing with a consort.<br /> <br /> As well as,<br /> <br /> Mottom with a pipe in one hand and the other playing towards assorted plates of food.<br /> <br /> Jadis in the background staring at a book rather than being involved in the proceedings.<br /> <br /> (Possibly) A very different looking Jagganoth boisterously enjoying himself while grinding his fist into the table.<br /> <br /> Solomon glancing up at the king above him with just a hint of affront.<br /> <br /> And Gob-Agog poised in a manner that implies her eyes are skimming over all of the others and her fingers twitching to snatch out.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm starting to wonder at the possibilities of their sympathetic backstories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-20-2015, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T07:57:25-07:00","id":521883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=521790#post521790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Will Ruins Everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what She Who Lives In Her Name said!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:34:05-07:00","id":521957,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... this may seem a little random, but has anyone considered that sleaze-bag boyfriend might be Incubus in disguise?<br /> <br /> He figures out where the 'chosen one' is, and representing Lust, seduces her - or at least plays her insecurities. At the same time, he directs his minions to chase the fleeing King, and when the King finds Alison not only is said King killed, but he is 'kidnapped' - thus setting off a chain of events that will make Alison kill his six other competitors and after that is done, take over everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1330-cyborg-stan","name":"Cyborg Stan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-20T09:57:18-07:00","id":521969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cyborg Stan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=521957#post521957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... this may seem a little random, but has anyone considered that sleaze-bag boyfriend might be Incubus in disguise?</div> </div> </div> </div>But they had Zaid floating above their table in suspended animation, during their little conference. It's true Incubus wasn't in attendance, but I think the other Demiurges would recognize him if he was secretly Zaid.<br 