d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T09:13:10-08:00","id":797381,"title":"","content":"People know he's got his eye half closed in that picture, right? That he's narrowing it while making a discerning facial expression? Perhaps post the picture directly to the left of it in which both of his eyes are open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T12:30:58-08:00","id":797458,"title":"","content":"I like how basically everything is a Raksha - angels and demons are both vortexes of reality-defying power, congealing into formless consciousness and wearing a mask of civility and shape. The names they go by may even (inversely?) correspond to the potency of one's Heart.<br /> <br /> Incubus is (I presume) the epitomy of the Assumption of Dreams and Passions tree, and is definitely drawing upon Alison's own subjective ideals and behaviors to more deeply entice her. I'd peg him as an Entertainer-Diplomat Ishvara, such that even his &quot;true&quot; shape is only as true as a Raksha's Assumptionless body.<br /> <br /> (I know there's no point in translating them to Exalted, but it's fun okay!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T13:35:38-08:00","id":797496,"title":"","content":"Minor objection. Angels rely on manufactured bodies to exist inside the Wheel the same way Demons require masks, both due to the unrestrained power of their soul-flame, which were made from the extremes of UN and YIS. But far as we know, the identities of angels are not tied to their bodies. It just happens that when they find themselves without one, it's likely they'll be killed and made to reincarnate, which resets their life cycle and personalities to an earlier stage. Because if they're long without a stone/whatever form, that probably means they have no way to acquire it and by extension no favors in the Void where they are vulnerable to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T09:56:13-08:00","id":797854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=797381#post797381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People know he's got his eye half closed in that picture, right? That he's narrowing it while making a discerning facial expression? Perhaps post the picture directly to the left of it in which both of his eyes are open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, &quot;his eyes are different sizes&quot; was totally my point.<br /> <br /> Come on, man.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T10:06:39-08:00","id":797856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=797854#post797854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, &quot;his eyes are different sizes&quot; was totally my point.<br /> <br /> Come on, man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to sound rude, but maybe you can explain your point? Many seem to miss it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T11:31:34-08:00","id":797887,"title":"","content":"I think Incubus looks like a fuck, and it amuses me to call Delicious sexier.<br /> <br /> (It also amuses me to say that Incubus looks like a fuck.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-01-2016, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T18:46:26-08:00","id":798545,"title":"","content":"Today. Mottom's palace, in the wonderful forest world of <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-45-to-3-46-mykos/#comments\" target=\"_blank\">Mykos</a>! A little less wonderful now, ever since Mottom took a liking to it's fruits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1516-solarious","name":"Solarious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-07T10:44:06-08:00","id":803209,"title":"","content":"New comic's been up for a while now. I'd been expecting people rabidly commenting about Alice's growing herodom, but since nobody mentioned the new page I'll <i>have </i>to do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-47/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/WON47.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-47/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wielder Of Names 3-47 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-47/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-47/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T05:29:23-08:00","id":805163,"title":"","content":"And another new page ... where we see Allison and Cio part ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-48/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/WON48.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-48/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wielder of Names 3-48 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-48/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-48/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T06:51:14-08:00","id":805206,"title":"","content":"I shouldn't be surprised that Cio isn't following Allison on what the devil believes is a suicide mission, but I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T08:55:37-08:00","id":805282,"title":"","content":"The comments on the comic page pointed out that Allison didn't bring her sword. While that's easy to see as a mistake, it might be a smart move. Allison has shown no evidence of proficiency with the weapon, and carrying it might easily be taken as a statement of hostile intent. Unless she can make it do work, leaving it behind may be the safer option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:01:35-08:00","id":808648,"title":"","content":"First impressions of a new world:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-49/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/WON49.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-49/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wielder of Names 3-49 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-49/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-49/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:11:31-08:00","id":808712,"title":"","content":"I wonder if that beast of burden is a Servant or just a man-faced animal.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, having a sapient slave for a steed is pretty decadent. On the other, a lumbering ape filling the cultural niche of the elephant is an interesting conceit. I think I'd prefer the latter, but we've seen evidence of the former practice in the Void.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 01-19-2016, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:52:01-08:00","id":808741,"title":"","content":"Massively important point in panel four:<br /> <br /> Mottom's goons are carrying <i>guns</i>.Looks like the seven are perfectly willing to use modern tech when they're not bound by the Throne treaty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T17:34:46-08:00","id":809248,"title":"","content":"I see he's released some new lore stuff to Patreon backers. Anything interesting there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T01:46:16-08:00","id":809445,"title":"","content":"Oh, so he has.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the last one was on the Servant race of Preem Vash, the Goblins. They were once the cleaners of the canals and sewers of Throne, and regarded as the garbage men of Creation. Their tight knit clan structure helped them in the formation of the first guilds. They lay clutches of eggs, and have three biological sexes (it's highly taboo to ask a goblin which sex it is). They have no eyes, but the sense of smell afforded by their face-sized nasal cavity is so acute that they can even detect emotional states through smelling chemical indicators; this makes them feared bargainers.<br /> <br /> The new card is about the Kind People, who you'll know as Mammon's race. They started off as Throne's couriers and guards, made to carry and protect all manner of goods. Thus, they're very hardy, require little food or rest, and their two sets of eyes can be controlled independently to give them a wide range of vision. Their mouth parts are sensitive and dextrous enough to be used as hands.<br /> <br /> Their families have a dual patriarch structure in which two males oversee the lives of numerous shared wives and offspring. They have a strict code of complicated ethics, and a caste system based on who they serve. Ones who serve powerful merchants have the highest rank in their society, above even those of kings.<br /> <br /> Oh, this is interesting; because they regard service to others as the highest calling, ones who seek power for themselves are treated as outcasts, and even attacked. Mammon is universally reviled as a demon by his own people.<br /> <br /> Their durability and constitution in battle gives them the moniker &quot;Dragons of the West&quot;, and while they dislike direct war, they have no hesitation about mercenary work, and many become knights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T02:50:02-08:00","id":809458,"title":"","content":"Sounds like an awesome basis for a non-human race in Exalted. Either a primordial one, or one created by First Age Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T10:04:57-08:00","id":809673,"title":"","content":"Thanks, man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The new card is about the Kind People, who you'll know as Mammon's race. They started off as Throne's couriers and guards, made to carry and protect all manner of goods. Thus, they're very hardy, require little food or rest, and their two sets of eyes can be controlled independently to give them a wide range of vision. Their mouth parts are sensitive and dextrous enough to be used as hands.<br /> <br /> Their families have a dual patriarch structure in which two males oversee the lives of numerous shared wives and offspring. They have a strict code of complicated ethics, and a caste system based on who they serve. Ones who serve powerful merchants have the highest rank in their society, above even those of kings.<br /> <br /> Oh, this is interesting; because they regard service to others as the highest calling, ones who seek power for themselves are treated as outcasts, and even attacked. Mammon is universally reviled as a demon by his own people.<br /> <br /> Their durability and constitution in battle gives them the moniker &quot;Dragons of the West&quot;, and while they dislike direct war, they have no hesitation about mercenary work, and many become knights. </div> </div> </div>Best Sustainers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T05:38:05-08:00","id":810587,"title":"","content":"A fortuitous (?) encounter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-50/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/WON50.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-50/\" target=\"_blank\"> Wielder of Names 3-50 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-50/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-3-50/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"use