ut to Quad. He's got 3 already and reaching for a 4th.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>New use for the coat of arms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T23:44:25-07:00","id":903303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=903133#post903133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> New use for the coat of arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering its usual wearer, I'm willing to bet it's not a new use at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T00:57:11-07:00","id":903321,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Offering</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Oh look, a tyrant giving their sob story to justify their tyranny. &quot;Oh, woe is me, heavy is the head that wears the crown! If only I could rid myself of the shackles of power!&quot;*<br /> <br /> I wish I was capable of giving a more eloquent response then punching her repeatedly and shouting &quot;BEING! A! VICTIM! DOESN'T! JUSTIFY! VICTIMIZING! YOU! EVIL! CALLOUS! GLUTTONOUS! CRUEL! WITCH!&quot;<br /> <br /> Ah well.<br /> <br /> *&quot;How hard have you tried?&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 05-30-2016, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T01:47:51-07:00","id":903334,"title":"","content":"It doesn't justify or excuse it, it merely makes it understandable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:22:55-07:00","id":903549,"title":"","content":"Good god this is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T19:35:37-07:00","id":903910,"title":"","content":"To quote a comment: &quot;Explains a lot, justifies nothing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T20:04:08-07:00","id":903920,"title":"","content":"Kinda lost interest in her character with this. Yes what happened to her was terrible, but at the same time it's just the same old &quot;woman abused by a man who then becomes powerful&quot; schtick that I've seen a dozen times before.<br /> <br /> At least her &quot;becomes powerful&quot; involves ruling a portion of the universe, so that's at least mildly interesting. More curious to see what Alison does at this point. She's been frustratingly passive so far, snark aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:13:47-07:00","id":903960,"title":"","content":"I think (based on what she's saying to Allison) that there's more going on here than just &quot;she was abused&quot;, especially since she doesn't emphasize that part very much.<br /> <br /> The more interesting part is that she makes it pretty clear that she <i>hates</i> being Mother Om. She hates her role as the perfect golden queen. Yet she (believes) she can't escape it, not without disrupting the equilibrium between the Demiurges and potentially destroying the entire multiverse.<br /> <br /> (Obviously this doesn't justify the fact that she's become an embittered decadent goddess-queen who takes her frustrations out with brutal gluttony on the worlds she rules as tyrant.)<br /> <br /> This also explains why she allows herself to appear old and withered among her peers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T01:29:33-07:00","id":904036,"title":"","content":"Hey, do people remember how many pages it took to explain the backstory of the universe?<br /> <br /> \u200bMaybe wait a bit before drawing conclusions, eh?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:03:12-07:00","id":904046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=903960#post903960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think (based on what she's saying to Allison) that there's more going on here than just &quot;she was abused&quot;, especially since she doesn't emphasize that part very much.<br /> <br /> The more interesting part is that she makes it pretty clear that she <i>hates</i> being Mother Om. She hates her role as the perfect golden queen. Yet she (believes) she can't escape it, not without disrupting the equilibrium between the Demiurges and potentially destroying the entire multiverse.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an interesting point; it gives me an idea in which Nadia's actions are not a response or retaliation to being elevated to Mother Om, but a kind of extreme extension of it. &quot;Oh, you want your beautiful mother goddess, bearer of the word Glory? I'll give you more of it than you can stomach.&quot; She devours world in order to fuel those extremes, as well as a kind of perverse replication of her own life's story.<br /> <br /> It depends on what we see has become of Hastet when Allison 'meets' him (which has not happened on this page, and so obviously we have not gotten the full story yet).<br /> <br /> I think the point of being trapped in her position is even more extreme; that at whatever point she became so disillusioned, the Universal War was happening around her, and somehow she can through it, leaving her with power over one-seventh of Creation by default.<br /> <br /> Between her and Jagganoth, I wonder if some or all of the Black Emperors might not be winners of a contest so much as survivors of a disaster. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T02:23:59-07:00","id":904051,"title":"","content":"I'm half convinced this is still an act she is putting on to manipulate Allison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T04:32:31-07:00","id":904081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=903910#post903910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To quote a comment: &quot;Explains a lot, justifies nothing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <img src=\"http://66.media.tumblr.com/440a7cee5d8e588f3d40da93c11d10a5/tumblr_inline_npi34jaiDU1rjrl4k_500.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:13:36-07:00","id":904437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=904046#post904046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between her and Jagganoth, I wonder if some or all of the Black Emperors might not be winners of a contest so much as survivors of a disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <i>believe</i> word of god is that they won because they cooperated with each other (hence the picture showing they were friends before the fall.) Presumably they somehow managed to have a shared friendship that most of the other Demiurges lacked.<br /> <br /> They're also, IIRC, all younger Demiurges. I would assume that this meant that they were quicker to understand what was going on, faster to bunker down and go to ground -- Mottom wouldn't have been one of the strongest Demiurges by a long shot, but she had a more realistic understanding of the nature of power and both the strengths and vulnerabilities of her position than the older ones, so she (and the other six) were probably the first to get together and say &quot;all right, we set up a parameter, hold as much as we can, let everyone else wear each other out and then wipe up the remains.&quot; Whereas the older Demiurges had been worshipped as omnipotent gods for so long that they didn't really get that they could lose or die until it happened.<br /> <br /> Or something along those lines. Someone like, say, Meti was probably howling like a madwoman and running around killing everyone with a sword. (Granted, based on her book Meti probably wanted to die anyway.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe Solomon and Jagganoth tanked while Jadis and Mammon buffed them, with Mottom standing behind them blasting you with thorns? And Gog-Agog or Incubus slipped in to stab you in the back? And the other Demiurges were all like &quot;omfg hax.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-31-2016, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T15:14:34-07:00","id":904490,"title":"","content":"I don't think Meti was a demiurge...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:25:40-07:00","id":904578,"title":"","content":"She was implied to be. Someone who looks very much like Maya, her only student, was shown fighting in the universal war (and Maya was once a &quot;conqueror of 20,000 worlds&quot; according to her pic on the artist's tumbr); Meti's sword manual also talks about the idiocy of her destiny-obsessed compatriots, which sounds a lot like the old Demiurges to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, unrelated, some power-level stuff from the tumblr: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This isn't so much an ask as it's a jokey speculation-explanation on KSBD power levels. Vegeta is inferior to Goku. Jugger-Star is Majin Vegeta, you compared Jagganoth to Goku/Superman levels of strength. All 6 Demiurges pooling their strength together is the only thing to match Jagganoths power. So that means the 7's combined power is equal to 2 Gokus. Zoss is superior in power and experience to the 7 in every way. So to answer other Anons question, Juggernaut Star is a cheap bastard. </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d put juggernaut at about \u00be of a Goku and Zoss somewhere from 5-7 Gokus. Allison is probably at 0.005 of a Goku, for reference. </div> </div> </div>That means that...<br /> <br /> Zoss: 5-7 Gokus.<br /> Jagganoth: 1 Goku.<br /> 6 Juggernaut Star: 0.75 Gokus.<br /> The other Demiurges: ~0.16 Gokus each.<br /> Allison: 0.005 Gokus.<br /> <br /> Mottom is only about 32 times as powerful as Allison right now. A lot, but not, like, in an entirely different class of existence.<br /> <br /> (Also he doesn't say at what point in Goku's timeline we're talking about, but if we assume somewhere early in DBZ, this would peg Allison's power level at somewhere over 45. On the other hand, if it's later, Allison's power level could be in the tens of thousands.)<br /> <br /> More seriously, the fact that 6 Juggernaut Star has significantly more personal power than Mottom seems like it might be about to become relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-31-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:37:33-07:00","id":904585,"title":"","content":"I love the fact that a Goku is now a unit of measurement for power levels, particularly because it's something Akira Toriyama originally introduced them in order to show how worthless they are.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I feel confidant in assuming that he's referring to late-series Goku, considering he's directly comparing him to superman.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 05-31-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:44:20-07:00","id":904593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=904578#post904578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She was implied to be. Someone who looks very much like Maya, her only student, was shown fighting in the universal war (and Maya was once a &quot;conqueror of 20,000 worlds&quot; according to her pic on the artist's tumbr); Meti's sword manual also talks about the idiocy of her destiny-obsessed compatriots, which sounds a lot like the old Demiurges to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a link to that exact page? I ask not because I don't believe you, but because atm I'm kicking myself for not noticing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:04:17-07:00","id":904604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=904593#post904593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have a link to that exact page? I ask not because I don't believe you, but because atm I'm kicking myself for not noticing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoops, not fighting in it, but obviously laid out in a way that links her to its beginnings. <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/ksbd-3-44/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>, in the second to last panel. Much thinner, but same skin tone, hair type, hair style (including the big white clip), and dresses very similarly to how she looks <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/?comic=ksbd-4-69\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Although it's not explicitly stated, I'd assume that Meti is pictured on the fan in the final panel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 05-31-2016, 09:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:12:27-07:00","id":904607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=904604#post904604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoops, not fighting in it, but obviously laid out in a way that links her to its beginnings. <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/ksbd-3-44/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>, in the second to last panel. Much thinner, but same skin tone, hair type, hair style (including the big white clip), and dresses very similarly to how she looks <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/?comic=ksbd-4-69\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Although it's not explicitly stated, I'd assume that Meti is pictured on the fan in the final panel.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T01:41:32-07:00","id":904790,"title":"","content":"Huh, cool. I think this is the first time when I actually get that there were several other demiurges beyond the ones we know about now. I'm sure it's been said, but it's just never been relevant before.<br /> <br /> Mottom is being deepened as a character and I think that's really cool. The &quot;cool motive, still murder&quot; meme is definitely in effect, but the comic is at least showing that she's not crazy, as such, just reacting to her situation in a way determined by her circumstances. I also really like that Allison turned young and is sitting at her feet. It feels like she's learning from Mottom.<br /> <br /> I personally think Mottom is still going to die, but I'd not object to her joining Allison's party, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=904578#post904578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She was implied to be. Someone who looks very much like Maya, her only student, was shown fighting in the universal war (and Maya was once a &quot;conqueror of 20,000 worlds&quot; according to her pic on the artist's tumbr); Meti's sword manual also talks about the idiocy of her destiny-obsessed compatriots, which sounds a lot like the old Demiurges to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, unrelated, some power-level stuff from the tumblr:<br /> That means that...<br /> <br /> Zoss: 5-7 Gokus.<br /> Jagganoth: 1 Goku.<br /> 6 Juggernaut Star: 0.75 Gokus.<br /> The other Demiurges: ~0.16 Gokus each.<br /> Allison: 0.005 Gokus.<br /> <br /> Mottom is only about 32 times as powerful as Allison right now. A lot, but not, like, in an entirely different class of existence.<br /> <br /> (Also he doesn't say at what point in Goku's timeline we're talking about, but if we assume somewhere early in DBZ, this would peg Allison's power level at somewhere over 45. On the other hand, if it's later, Allison's power level could be in the tens of thousands.)<br /> <br /> More seriously, the fact that 6 Juggernaut Star has significantly more personal power than Mottom seems like it might be about to become relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't know. 32 times more powerful is pretty damn huge deal. I oversaw a complete newbie bench pressing a while ago, and they managed about 42 kg. From what I could find in five minutes of googling, the world record is at about 400 kg. That difference between complete newbie and world record holder is still &quot;just&quot; 10 times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T02:25:53-07:00","id":904802,"title":"","content":"There were a huge number of them. I'm not sure it's said how many, but every world has a gate, and every gate has a key, which would mean 777,777 demiurges, assuming every key once had an owner (which isn't necessarily true, but I'd assume it's near that figure, at least.) Most of them died in the cataclysmic war until only the current seven were left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T03:49:11-07:00","id":904837,"title":"","content":"I doubt any of the Seven were ever friends, or even cooperated. If anything, they're mortal enemies who happen to have become each other's only peers.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on the subject of demiurges:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There were less than ten thousand Demiurges to start, which grew into a much larger society once the worlds were opened up to Throne. A lot of the demiurges of Zoss\u2019 time were considered the old guard or elders of the demiurges, who formed its ruling council and the core decision making group of the Concordance (the huge debate hall where they ruled democratically - with Zoss\u2019 oversight of course).<br /> <br /> The expansion of the demiurges came with people from outlying worlds or the offspring of those in Throne. They became demiurges through ambition or power, either inherited or seized. These new demiurges were not of the original cadre that broke into Throne, and tended to be slightly weaker in their power and looser in their moral codes. This expansion was so extreme that by the time the second conquest was at it\u2019s zenith and the Universal War was starting, the population of demiurges in Throne was closer to two or three million. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T07:08:06-07:00","id":904936,"title":"","content":"Yes, an impromptu description of relative<br /> strengths definitely adheres to that level of mathematical rigour. Yeesh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T09:52:00-07:00","id":905025,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-88/\" target=\"_blank\">New Page!</a><br /> <br /> This (and the last page) does explain a lot of Nadia's worldview, as she's presented it. She always seemed very fatalistic for a reality-warping goddess-queen ruler of a thousand worlds. This helps explain though.<br /> <br /> From a very young age, she became used to the idea that the world held more power over her than she did over it. It was something that couldn't be fought or beaten. Society was something to be bowed to.<br /> <br /> And now, for all her power, despite being a new god and ruling over thousands of worlds, she's not really any more free from society's expectations than she ever was. I only imagine that reinforced her views- no matter how powerful she becomes, there's no way to escape. It's inevitable, so she might as well dissolve into hedonistic splendor.<br /> <br /> I feel like despite this, Nadia is very honest about her role in things. She's, as she said, a coward. I especially remember how she mocked Solomon for thinking that he was still a hero. I feel like she understands exactly how reprehensible she is; just doesn't think it matters anymore.<br /> <br /> But yeah, it's nice to get insight into the antagonist, but that doesn't make them any less terrible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T11:45:05-07:00","id":905078,"title":"","content":"Yes, it's interesting that it's not about vengeance, but the powers that boil just beneath her.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also find it to be a good instance of something that I think could make a strong story in Exalted. Just imagine a Solar rising to power over the Scarlet Dynasty and needing to struggle against their demands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T12:49:30-07:00","id":905112,"title":"","content":"I find it interesting that the number of demiurges exceed the number of keys and that keys do not seem to contribute significantly to personal power. We know that the keys literally act as keys to individual gates and that they appear to have allowed All-Yis-Un to mask a demon without actually knowing what she was doing, but not much else. I had thought that the gift of his key was what made Zoss vulnerable to Juggernaut, but perhaps it was just that he was being chased by a pack of thorns while injured and somewhat surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:18:21-07:00","id":905171,"title":"","content":"I've got to know, is this &quot;Al-Yis-Un&quot; thing something that has picked up in the part of the fandom that comments on the comics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:22:04-07:00","id":905175,"title":"","content":"Maybe this could be a motivation for the Empress herself. Always afraid of her descendants.<br /> <br /> No wonder she ran away*<br /> <br /> <br /> *now my second favorite Scarlet Empress theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:27:14-07:00","id":905178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905175#post905175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this could be a motivation for the Empress herself. Always afraid of her descendants.<br /> <br /> No wonder she ran away*<br /> <br /> <br /> *now my second favorite Scarlet Empress theory.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/3Yf7haP.png\" target=\"_blank\">headcannon</a> is that she's sitting in a beach chair next to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/778406-quick-n-dirty-exalted-sketch?p=778410#post778410\">Kejak watching naked Exalts play volleyball.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:39:54-07:00","id":905192,"title":"","content":"^bitch took my seat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T14:39:54-07:00","id":905193,"title":"","content":"My impression is that Mottom styles herself a prisoner so that she can consider herself blameless. After all, it's the system that's making her do this. It's a gilded cage made out of gold she wants. If she was to rock it, she would lose what she had. And that's probably true, but she would also be free of her own imagined prison.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905078#post905078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it's interesting that it's not about vengeance, but the powers that boil just beneath her.<br /> <br /> \u200bI also find it to be a good instance of something that I think could make a strong story in Exalted. Just imagine a Solar rising to power over the Scarlet Dynasty and needing to struggle against their demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. You become a leader when people decide to follow you. Even if you could overpower everyone, it kind of defeats the point of ruling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905112#post905112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it interesting that the number of demiurges exceed the number of keys and that keys do not seem to contribute significantly to personal power. We know that the keys literally act as keys to individual gates and that they appear to have allowed All-Yis-Un to mask a demon without actually knowing what she was doing, but not much else. I had thought that the gift of his key was what made Zoss vulnerable to Juggernaut, but perhaps it was just that he was being chased by a pack of thorns while injured and somewhat surprised.</div> </div> </div> </div>The keys are certainly mysterious. As you say, I don't think possessing one gives Power Level +5 passively, but it certainly does do something, as Allison has proven. I myself wonder if Mottom's become-a-tree spell are due to her using her key, or if they're her own magic that's been empowered by the key (or maybe not even that). The keys certainly has a social implication as well, giving their wielders lots of time and resources to develop their personal talents if nothing else, but that privilege is also in the end bought through power. It seems to be a complex system of causes and effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905171#post905171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got to know, is this &quot;Al-Yis-Un&quot; thing something that has picked up in the part of the fandom that comments on the comics?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mostly see it spelled Allis-Un or Alice-Un, but the idea of Allison's name being read as the name of god seems to be fairly established.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 06-01-2016, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T17:12:18-07:00","id":905272,"title":"","content":"It's funny: when I first saw Mottom, I was worried we were going to get an instance in which a woman rises to power and then uses that to overindulge to the point of becoming decrepit.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen, when we saw her holding court for the first time, I was worried we were going to get an instance of a sorceress who glamours herself up to look younger and prettier out of vanity.<br /> <br /> Seeing how rambunctious she was around Allison (and recalling it at the Concordance) eased that a bit, but...<br /> <br /> In light of this last statement, I think that those occasions in which she gets to be alone with herself and her peers are occasions in which she revels in ugliness and vulgarity.<br /> <br /> That, contrary to being vain, she's happiest when she feels relaxed enough to allow herself to look as far from that glimmering jewel as possible; that when she looks like that, she's being herself, and it's the closest thing she can get to liking herself.<br /> <br /> Not even as a case of some kind of rebellious self-mortification, just... very old.<br /> <br /> That's rather delightful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:08:43-07:00","id":905294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905272#post905272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny: when I first saw Mottom, I was worried we were going to get an instance in which a woman rises to power and then uses that to overindulge to the point of becoming decrepit.<br /> <br /> \u200bThen, when we saw her holding court for the first time, I was worried we were going to get an instance of a sorceress who glamours herself up to look younger and prettier out of vanity.<br /> <br /> Seeing how rambunctious she was around Allison (and recalling it at the Concordance) eased that a bit, but...<br /> <br /> In light of this last statement, I think that those occasions in which she gets to be alone with herself and her peers are occasions in which she revels in ugliness and vulgarity.<br /> <br /> That, contrary to being vain, she's happiest when she feels relaxed enough to allow herself to look as far from that glimmering jewel as possible; that when she looks like that, she's being herself, and it's the closest thing she can get to liking herself.<br /> <br /> Not even as a case of some kind of rebellious self-mortification, just... very old.<br /> <br /> That's rather delightful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice she still have the golden hair though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:51:40-07:00","id":905316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905294#post905294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notice she still have the golden hair though.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWhat, when she's old?<br /> <br /> I... don't think she does?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T19:49:34-07:00","id":905342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905316#post905316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWhat, when she's old?<br /> <br /> I... don't think she does?</div> </div> </div> </div>Before she eats, its under her headscarf. Although looking back it might have gone grey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T21:18:27-07:00","id":905395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=903321#post903321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Offering</a><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> *&quot;How hard have you tried?&quot;</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing keeping the Demiurges from tearing each other apart is the seven of the having a number of universe, in a demented M.A.D scenario. Mottom calls it quits, those worlds are up for grabs and the remaining six go to war.<br /> &quot;How Hard have you tried?&quot; Tried to do what, kick off a multiversal slaughterhouse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T22:22:13-07:00","id":905411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=905395#post905395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing keeping the Demiurges from tearing each other apart is the seven of the having a number of universe, in a demented M.A.D scenario. Mottom calls it quits, those worlds are up for grabs and the remaining six go to war.<br /> &quot;How Hard have you tried?&quot; Tried to do what, kick off a multiversal slaughterhouse?</div> </div> </div> </div>The woman can turn a man into a <i>tree</i>. If she wanted to find a way to stop being a horrible scourge upon the universe without tearing it to pieces, she probably could.<br /> <br /> I mean, no, finding a way to give power to someone who'll use it wisely and well whilst not plunging the multiverse into darkness is not even remotely simple or easy, but she's been doing this for what, centuries? Millennia? <i>She can figure this out</i>.<br /> <br /> It's obvious the only thing stopping her from being a protector instead of a destroyer, is her.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>What if she's trying to pawn her power and the consequences of the war off on Allison.</i> Holy criminy!<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh wow, that's a precarious cold war scenario that's going to end badly. I never liked doing this much anyway, so I should get out of here while the getting's good. Now let's see, where's my way out...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, look at that. A young, uncertain, but still morally clean heroine whose very existence breaks the stalemate? That'll do nicely...&quot;</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 06-02-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:03:01-07:00","id":905455,"title":"","content":"Also a lot of these assumptions are based on information that Mottom herself has supplied. It could well be that the other 6 demi-urges only just manage to keep her in check. This may all be an attempt for her to spin a narrative to her own ends to manipulate the bearer of the Key of Kings. I think there is a lot more to this exposition than meets the eye. Especially remembering the woman we met at the concordance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:21:14-07:00","id":905490,"title":"","content":"That Jagganoth is invincible and kept in check only by the combined efforts of the other six is something that Abaddon stated a few times before it was ever brought up in the comic.<br /> <br /> He's also repeatedly alluded to the backstories of the demiurges in a manner that makes me find it unlikely that this reveal is anything other than what it appears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T02:53:38-07:00","id":905506,"title":"","content":"Yes. If you follow the <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">tumblr</a> for the comic, the author has repeatedly indicated that most of the Demiurges (and Mottom in particular) have a tragic backstory. Of course, the fact that she became exactly the sort of tyrant she hates is part of the tragedy. (She even references it herself when telling Allison what will happen to her.)<br /> <br /> He's also repeatedly hinted that the story isn't going to be about Allison <i>fighting</i> the Demiurges per se. (I think that Ciocie's planning about training montages and magic swords was mostly supposed to be a joke about how people would leap straight to that assumption, and the kind of story where it's all about making Allison as optimal as possible so she can cut off the Demiurges' heads.)<br /> <br /> Beyond that, going &quot;haha, jk, it was all a lie&quot; would undermine this last scene with Allison confronting her in particular.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 06-02-2016, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T03:19:54-07:00","id":905518,"title":"","content":"Fair Dinkum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/669-hermes12","name":"Hermes12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T01:44:41-07:00","id":907032,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New page</a>. Of course that would be what it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T09:12:03-07:00","id":907127,"title":"","content":"I love Aesma's stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:15:19-07:00","id":912072,"title":"","content":"Those manly priests really really should have taken a moment to ask who exactly she fell in love with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T21:35:00-07:00","id":912078,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-91/\" target=\"_blank\">New Page!</a><br /> <br /> (Also Aesma falls in love and reacts with nuclear explosions and even more extreme measures.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T22:12:34-07:00","id":912093,"title":"","content":"Something interesting I read while perusing the<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.tumblr.com/post/142578279665/so-cio-was-renamed-when-she-was-demoted-right\" target=\"_blank\"> K6BD tumblr. </a><br /> <br /> A theory that Cio's name spells out Coca Cola.<br /> <br /> If Ciocie &quot;Cio&quot; Cioelle is pronounced as <i>See-oh-ci-a See-oh See-oh-ell-a</i>, that is. Certainly an amusing idea, at the very least. (Though a bit contentious I feel.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T02:03:24-07:00","id":912161,"title":"","content":"So that's where all the girls go, I guess.<br /> <br /> By the way, notice the object in Hastet Om's hand on the previous page. Turns out it didn't <i>start</i> as a fork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T03:41:53-07:00","id":912182,"title":"","content":"Even Mottom has used that thing as her staff of office when she's in public, and Abaddon has previously identified it as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T05:12:08-07:00","id":91219