ue":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T10:56:16-07:00","id":994674,"title":"","content":"I just didn't recognize our dear Princess Mamoru Etc. I thought she was, wossname, Cio's ex from the drinking contest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T23:19:57-07:00","id":995094,"title":"","content":"No, the pipe was a dead giveaway.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how much White Chain tells them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T01:12:08-07:00","id":995113,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New comic.</a><br /> <br /> It just doesn't seem to occur to these people that Allison was the intended recipient all along. I wonder why?<br /> <br /> Unknown blood relation? Translation error in a prophecy?<br /> <br /> Or maybe King Zoss just changed his mind. After all, a true Sovereign doesn't let a little thing like Fate boss them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 10-29-2016, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T10:52:32-07:00","id":995260,"title":"","content":"I can imagine it now :<br /> <br /> Alisson: Zoss, why me?<br /> Zoss: because they're all huge sexists and would never think a woman could be my heir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T17:02:11-07:00","id":995435,"title":"","content":"We don't know for <i>sure</i> that Zoss chose her; his words are extremely cryptic.<br /> <br /> But based on what he's said, I think that he would be contemptuous of the idea of being &quot;chosen&quot; at all. Allison was chosen because she was there, but the important part is whether she chooses herself based on her actions afterwards. <i>That</i> is why he addresses her as the successor.<br /> <br /> It should be immediately obvious that true royalty isn't something you bestow on someone.<br /> <br /> (If I had to guess the story's ending, I would not be surprised if it's a bit like <i>Aesma and the Red-Eyed King</i> where Allison gives the key to her boyfriend, he turns out to be a jerk, then she beats him up anyway and takes it back - or beats him up and doesn't bother to take it back because the key isn't really important compared to True Royalty; once you understand the true name of god yourself, you don't need a tuning fork.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-29-2016, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T03:35:58-07:00","id":995572,"title":"","content":"\u201cIn some parts they know the master of Throne as the god Zayus Patrom, father of lightning. In others they know him as the great warrior called Angel-Breaker, who fights with a spear dipped in molten silver. Only one name is bestowed upon him in common across all the wretched cosmos: King.\u201d<br /> -Sayophraxes, Silent Sister of the Wax Covenant<br /> <br /> Dude. Fighting with a spear dipped in molten silver is precisely the sort of thing my Ysr sorcerer (or any Resources 4+ Solar) would do. Summon some fire elementals to carry and heat the raw materials, dip your Longfang in molten silver, and transform your enemies into (briefly) living artwork of silver kintsugi as you slay them.<br /> <br /> How would you run this, not only as a gimmick for a stunt, but as a tactic that could be repeated over and over again? It seems like you'd need Craft(Combat Taxidermy) or something else really ridiculous in order to make true artwork out of their remains, and that would also help with the preservation of their corpses. Does this warrant custom charms? A weapon specific to the task? It seems like leaving a trail of molten silver wherever your weapon strikes would do aggravated damage instead of lethal, but this is definitely not a subject directly addressed in the rules. Opinions?<br /> <br /> Actually, forget the sorcerer, I'm turning this guy into a Deathknight for my campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:19:09-07:00","id":995696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=995572#post995572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you run this, not only as a gimmick for a stunt, but as a tactic that could be repeated over and over again? It seems like you'd need Craft(Combat Taxidermy) or something else really ridiculous in order to make true artwork out of their remains, and that would also help with the preservation of their corpses. Does this warrant custom charms? A weapon specific to the task? It seems like leaving a trail of molten silver wherever your weapon strikes would do aggravated damage instead of lethal, but this is definitely not a subject directly addressed in the rules. Opinions?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally treat dipping it molten silver as a +4L on a Decisive that lasts a turn and then cools off and ruins the efficiency of your blade unless you've successfully struck flesh or dipped it again.<br /> <br /> Aggravated seems overkill to me, unless sorcery is involved in Working a magical cauldron carried aback a Furnace-Rhino palanquin which endows the silver within it with the insatiable hunger of Hesiesh and consumes all lesser weapons thrown within it (i.e. non-artifact weapons become one-shot use, only artifact weapons &quot;survive&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T10:48:54-07:00","id":995705,"title":"","content":"Sounds to me like an Evocation, unless you want to make some kind of Craft-Melee hybrid Charmtree.<br /> Also, it occurs to me that the &quot;molten silver&quot; is probably an interpretation of that white lightning-fire Allison used to kill murder tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T11:46:24-07:00","id":996179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=995696#post995696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally treat dipping it molten silver as a +4L on a Decisive that lasts a turn and then cools off and ruins the efficiency of your blade unless you've successfully struck flesh or dipped it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be <i>very</i> cautious about anything that directly adds lethal to decisive attacks, since it has the potential to make &quot;spam decisive attacks, ignore initiative&quot; a viable strategy. It shows up sometimes, but you want to make sure it's not something that can easily be repeated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T08:30:29-07:00","id":996612,"title":"","content":"Jeez, what do people have against stunts all of a sudden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T10:06:06-07:00","id":996665,"title":"","content":"Interesting. The Zoss/Zeus parallel gets stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T17:53:00-07:00","id":996907,"title":"","content":"Has no one considered that Zoss killed the Prime Angels and literally nailed Metatron to the ground? Why does the bloated bag of ash think its plans rise to height of mattering to those on the level of the Conquering King?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T18:36:02-07:00","id":996920,"title":"","content":"If I was indulging the curious value judgements, I would think in terms of how Metatron has been described as being outside causality, a Royalist, and fixated on the idea of reality being confined to cycles.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would note how Metatron's plan for the Successor is to be brought back to him for instruction, which is an approximation of what happened the first time around. It could still be seen as a form of subservience, albeit one that enforces itself over and over again.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T11:25:51-07:00","id":997264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=995113#post995113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New comic.</a><br /> <br /> It just doesn't seem to occur to these people that Allison was the intended recipient all along. I wonder why?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really an answer, but this was posted on the K6BD tumblr:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Q: Out of curiosity, why do people automatically assume that Allison was an accident, rather then them misinterpreting the prophecy?<br /> A: White chain believes that because Metatron and Juggernaut and Michael all believe so. That\u2019s basically what it comes down to.</b></span></div>We haven't learned why they believe Zaid to be the successor, though, but I doubt it comes down to sexism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T19:00:14-07:00","id":998551,"title":"","content":"&quot;Fate is not a cage except for those who fear it.<br /> <br /> A true Ruler is the <b>Wielder of Names</b>. By names <i>she</i> cuts the world as <i>she</i> pleases, and <i>she</i> cuts <b><i>herself</i></b> into greater forms still.<br /> <br /> <i>She</i> is not shaped by the world, but instead becomes the <b>Shaper</b>.<br /> <br /> There's work to be done. What shape will you choose, hm?<br /> <br /> Will you chose to be a king?&quot;<br /> italics mine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-5-95/\" target=\"_blank\">Zoss</a><br /> <br /> Jadis gained her prophetic power because she saw the Shape of the Universe. Metatron foresaw the handoff from Zoss to the successor.<br /> <br /> In effect, what Zoss is saying is that for the true king Prophecy is a load of rot. Zaid may very well have been the &quot;chosen one.&quot; Zoss doesn't give a damn, even using female pronouns to show this was meant for Alison. Alison shouldn't give a damn either.<br /> <br /> If she had chosen to remain a peasant than should would be a meat-puppet keeping the key warm for the true successor. Since she chose to be a king she made herself the true successor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T22:36:09-07:00","id":998621,"title":"","content":"My prediction is that if Allison was meant to be the queen after all, then when the moment passes and everyone realizes it was Allison all along, she's shocked for exactly one second. Then she grips her key, smirks, and goes &quot;You're goddamn right.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:07:24-07:00","id":998743,"title":"","content":"Talent<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-1-5/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/SOT5.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-1-5/\" target=\"_blank\"> Seeker of Thrones 1-5 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-1-5/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-1-5/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:39:02-07:00","id":999089,"title":"","content":"This just underscores the degree of gluttony, here. I doubt Nyave is the only one of the girls presented to Mottom who was profoundly exceptional in some manner--Abbadon mentioned having stories in mind for all of them.<br /> <br /> And in the end, they weren't going to be anything more than the scores of plates at empty tables when Allison and Nadia talk privately--to be consumed and wasted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T02:09:47-08:00","id":999130,"title":"","content":"I like that desk lamp in the 8th panel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T15:23:45-08:00","id":999457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=999089#post999089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This just underscores the degree of gluttony, here. I doubt Nyave is the only one of the girls presented to Mottom who was profoundly exceptional in some manner--Abbadon mentioned having stories in mind for all of them.<br /> <br /> And in the end, they weren't going to be anything more than the scores of plates at empty tables when Allison and Nadia talk privately--to be consumed and wasted.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA small number of them apparently get recruited to serve as her dames, although I wouldn't know if that was from every tribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T05:49:55-08:00","id":1000725,"title":"","content":"You're hired,<br /> <br /> <div 