px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Damn. I wasn't expecting that after all that talk about being soft. This just makes Juggarnaut more awesome. Buck the cultural trends! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T05:07:38-08:00","id":1030007,"title":"","content":"So he pulled a Nasu then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2626-yzarc","name":"Yzarc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:50:21-08:00","id":1030163,"title":"","content":"And here I thought there was not more to unfold so much as elaborate on past Juggernaut's vapid nihilistic jackassitude.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Color me <i>extremely </i>surprised, and not just because she (he, it?) appears to be breaking the rules really hard by making a body of fire within the Wheel. Angels need to be contained in a vessel, and as an extension of an existing body she technically is but at the same time not. Quoting someone I discussed this with, she is a paradox. A sudden human aspect to Juggernaut also implies a malleability that is not natural to Angels, and let's not even get started how the wheel-body was in the Void too. This can all probably be attributed to JS's special attributes, but the meaning of those and what they constitute exactly are what's truly thought-provoking.<br /> <br /> The &quot;I'm tired&quot; felt <i>exceptionally real</i>, and I'm reminded of her earlier conversation with White Chain and how Abbadon has commented that Juggernaut Star is one of the few who have learned the truth of the universe and their beliefs and methods are strongly shaped by that.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T13:23:29-08:00","id":1030215,"title":"","content":"I think Juggernaut hates White Chain because White Chain is like a much younger and more innocent Juggernaut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:48:55-08:00","id":1032206,"title":"","content":"Exceptionally pleased that the giant baby (!!!) survived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:06:40-08:00","id":1032905,"title":"","content":"The page has changed! It originally had Maya ask about the face and Juggernaut appear not to know what she was talking about. Now it is all Juggernaut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:30:20-08:00","id":1032914,"title":"","content":"Hee. I always like it when I see webcomic artists correcting themselves as they go.<br /> <br /> It makes me feel so much better about my numerous errors and sneaky corrections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:48:37-08:00","id":1038083,"title":"","content":"So, we're seeing more of Incubus, and I'm finding him to be a rather interesting take on a villain.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's funny that when Abbadon once said that he was gay for ambition, the most obvious reading would have been for the idea that Incubus had a lust for the accumulation of power for himself, but what it actually seems to mean is that he gets off on seeing and facilitating the ambitions of other people.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm guessing that Incubus himself is a rather hollow person, devoid of dreams and with no real sense of what to do with power after having acquired it, so he alleviates his ennui by finding other people and infusing them with drive and strength and living vicariously through them chasing their dreams.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's interesting in its own right, but I'm also finding it to have some good resonances with and inspirations for Exalted concerning matters of the raksha and possibly the Infernal Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:23:50-08:00","id":1038147,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Incubus will be the one Alison spends time with this voljme, and the set up to Mammon will wind up bejng delayed to next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:27:04-08:00","id":1038152,"title":"","content":"I think we're going to get a couple of books including more than one demiurge, especially since the role of Incubus doesn't seem quite straightforwardly antagonistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:21:25-08:00","id":1038495,"title":"","content":"Do you think accepting his offer to unlock her potential would impose more of an actual or metaphorical leash on All-Yis-Un? I assume she is going to turn him down, but I can't tell if Incubus is the type who would impose something like a devil kiss or similar back door. It might be more along the lines of the ability to take back what he did or a psychological hold based on obligation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T14:37:37-08:00","id":1038586,"title":"","content":"Given the description of Incubus' domain as an anarchy, and my own assumptions about his personality, I don't think that's how he, personally rolls. Maybe it's a way that distributing portions of their power can work that some of the others can go with, but I think Incubus just gives people shortcuts to their own self-actualization (which then undermines the experience of achieving it), and then unleashes them to run rampant in the worlds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T15:32:48-08:00","id":1038612,"title":"","content":"IIRC the author has said there will be five volumes, so (unless that plan changes) we're not going to get a one-demiurge-per-volume thing the way some people expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T02:55:01-08:00","id":1039329,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Well, that happened</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2626-yzarc","name":"Yzarc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T03:35:31-08:00","id":1039339,"title":"","content":"I think he will come to regret this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:41:04-08:00","id":1041964,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-4-27/\" target=\"_blank\">New Offering</a>.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T13:40:07-08:00","id":1042003,"title":"","content":"Considering that he has a first consort, I wonder if Incubus still meets with people directly, or conducts all of his business through dreams.<br /> <br /> I like his long hair, for how it gives him that kind of hermit look.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the description of him is not incompatible with my suppositions that he's desensitized and lives vicariously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T14:11:19-08:00","id":1042024,"title":"","content":"So, three shekels on &quot;dream vampire&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T16:28:00-08:00","id":1042109,"title":"","content":"I just think it's interesting that his word is Flame and not Dream or something. Then again, I wouldn't have guessed Glory for Mottom either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T17:56:21-08:00","id":1042139,"title":"","content":"So here's how I'm assuming all this works. Incubus has a problem that needs dealing with. Incubus goes hunting through people's dreams for someone who:<br /> A. Is also affected negatively by whatever Incubus is having a problem with<br /> B. Is essentially powerless against whatever Incubus is having a problem with<br /> C. Is aware of their powerlessness in the face of said whatever<br /> <br /> When Incubus finds someone that hits these three criteria, he offers to use his<b><span style=\"color:#FFA07A\"> FLAME</span></b> to light a fire within them. Suddenly there's someone right in the middle of whatever problem that Incubus wants dealt with who not only has world shaking power, but also a little copy of one of the universe's seven god kings showing them how to use it in their minds. Generally whatever problem Incubus had is either resolved in fairly short order, in which case Incubus has a fairly loyal servant because he helped them achieve their goal of dealing with the problem, or the exalted servant burns themselves out, which probably damages whatever the problem was enough for him to try again with other methods.<br /> <br /> Assuming the pawn succeeds, they have in them an advisor who is probably a super good manipulator that they already trust, so when Incubus aims them at another problem similar to the one they had to deal with before, they're likely to jump at the chance to deal with it again. And if they don't deal with it well? Assuming he can't just snatch the power back at will, the advisor clams up and suddenly there's all this power they have that they can't use because the advisor in their head was doing all the work managing it for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:15:46-08:00","id":1042145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ellis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1042109#post1042109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think it's interesting that his word is Flame and not Dream or something. Then again, I wouldn't have guessed Glory for Mottom either.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things are probably a bit more allegorical.<br /> <br /> For reference, the seven divine words are Glory, Tower, Flame, Diamond, Blade, Mind, and Beast.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TidyGamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incubus has a problem that needs dealing with.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWelll... Abbadon has described Incubus' domain as an anarchy consisting of endless battles for dominion by warlords who are hand raised by him.<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel that implies less of a function-oriented selection process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:09:34-08:00","id":1042169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1042145#post1042145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For reference, the seven divine words are Glory, Tower, Flame, Diamond, Blade, Mind, and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still wondering who has what, in regards to those words.<br /> <br /> Glory - Mottom.<br /> Tower - Gog Agog? The Tower likely represents the unspoken Seventh Syllable of Royalty and thus seems appropriate for a creature with a uniquely weird sense of self, such as a sentient pile of worms. Jagganoth? He's being set up as the 'Big Bad' and the 'I' seems to be the final Syllable. Jadis? According to Abaddon, she has seen the Shape of Creation; which is to say the Wheel, which turned on its side becomes the Tower.<br /> Flame - Incubus.<br /> Diamond - Jagganoth? Diamonds are unbreakable, so is Jaggs. Mammon? Diamonds are precious shiny things. Solomon? I don't know.<br /> Blade - Jagganoth? Seems pretty straightforward. Solomon? It makes me think of the 'cut the baby in half' story. Mammon? The Blade of Want seems appropriate to the King of Greed.<br /> Mind - Solomon? He strikes me as a planner and schemer, but also one who is notable for having grand designs. Jadis? She's almost omniscient and doesn't have much left except her mind.<br /> Beast - Jagganoth? He does seem like one of the more monstrous demiurges. Gog-Agog? Envy is basically petty hatred, which is especially beastly to me. Mammon? He's the most monstrous in seeming.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:28:32-08:00","id":1042179,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't want to speculate very much, but I tentatively suppose that Beast might be Mammon's word, not so much for his being as the connotations the word has to materialism, in a certain biblical sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Blade of Want seems appropriate to the King of Greed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't think Blade of Want refers to the desire to possess things, I think it refers to the terrible existential dilemma of the desire for meaning and purpose, with the blade both serving as a tool to impose your will on the substance of creation and a means of ultimately becoming at peace with your own finite existence.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Blade of Want signifies Royalty, and the path to achieving it is something that all of them have stalled on.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think the frequent attribution of divinity to Cutting, itself reflected in the concept of Blade of Want, is why the term is among the divine words, but it is only an incomplete fragment. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T16:31:50-08:00","id":1044767,"title":"","content":"The newest page should provide sufficient context as to why the word of Incubus is Flame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:23:01-08:00","id":1044802,"title":"","content":"So, seems he's a crack seller","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T18:41:18-08:00","id":1044809,"title":"","content":"So it seems as though Incubus' deal is that he's burned out on the power of his own Flame, so he portions it out and imbues it in people with big dreams and weak wills so that they'll go out and live on his behalf.<br /> <br /> \u200bEventually, they burn out as well, and come crawling back to him begging for some reinvigoration. Maybe he can give it to them a few times, maybe he can't, but one way or another they're left incapable and just hang around in the filth of his domain, scrounging about and trying to get whatever shreds of stimulation they can.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find it quite amusing that he chides these people whom he has given the status of kings as though they were errant children. That they're around makes me think that Incubus might lack the drive to even go as far as kill them or cast them out.<br /> <br /> \u200bIncidentally, one will notice that his throne room contains a call back to the image of him shown in the page depicting Throne in profile (which is numerically, if not chronologically, his first appearance).<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's funny, I went back to that page to check if the name of his pit was referred to there, noticed the image of him seated on his throne with blood trickling from his mouth while slaves before him crawl forward with filled goblets and an enormous mound of them lie empty behind him, and assumed it was metaphorical.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut no, his throne is indeed surrounded by huge piles of empty goblets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T21:33:14-08:00","id":1044883,"title":"","content":"Lol, i notice you say he gives power to those with big dreams and weak wills.....<br /> <br /> So he's in for a big kick in the ass when he finds Allison is the oppisite. She has shown no real ambition. Purpose, but not ambition. But when push comes to shove, she can be rather willful.<br /> <br /> He's gonna regret what he did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T22:34:42-08:00","id":1044915,"title":"","content":"I think he's already set up for Allison being a bit different from his usual clientele, given that Zoss put the Master Key in her head.<br /> <br /> Incubus says he wants an ally, but I think he might just want to ride the final high of their whole system being torn down around him.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just in the sense of assisting the Successor; if I'm right about him almost literally living vicariously through his subjects, then a piece of himself might mean that her own achievements get fed into him directly.<br /> <br /> Mind, I still think he's in for some disappointment, if she turns out to not be what he hoped she was.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would also represent an interesting parallel to Mottom, and possibly a setup for what might be the deal with all of the Seven; if they really do think that Jadis is never wrong, and Jadis has predicted their downfall, then some of them might just want to go down on their own terms (which in the case of Mottom seemed to include finding a way to be set aside without needing to die).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T22:50:19-08:00","id":1044927,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-4-28-king-of-the-pit/\" target=\"_blank\">New Offering</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T22:52:38-08:00","id":1044929,"title":"","content":"You're a bit late. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-06T23:12:06-08:00","id":1044938,"title":"","content":"I got a feeling that Incubus is the Ultimate Hedonist. He spent so much time getting high on pretty much everything he could think of, all he's got left is the thrill of finding new thrills. And that's would make so much sense: he empowers other to find their own thrills and vicariously getting high by proxy - with the added bonus of enjoying even the catastrophic failures, because, hey, no skin off HIS back.<br /> <br /> This could also explain why he went to Allisson - sure, she's different, and likely deadly to him, but that's exactly the point - she's a complete unknown to his own outlook on life. Who can tell what she's gonna cook up? And if she DOES end up taking him out? Hey, that's another explosive scenario to enjoy! Hell, for all we know, he's gonna go down getting off the new and novel experience of defeat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:26:59-08:00","id":1045547,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-4-29/\" target=\"_blank\">The Lord of the Pit bares the blemishes of his soul as well</a>.<br /> <br /> And I believe the proper coloquialism to react to this arrangement is &quot;oh, fuck&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T19:00:14-08:00","id":1045562,"title":"","content":"Huh, already?<br /> <br /> Oh, turns out I was wrong about something.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with it coming out like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T02:00:45-08:00","id":1045656,"title":"","content":"I definitely didn't see it coming, but it looks like he's talking about Maya, isn't he? I can't imagine there are that many fat, washed-up perpetually-drunk former Demiurges who were once legendary generals who ruled 20,000 worlds. It didn't occur to me that the &quot;remnants of the most powerful army in the universe&quot; that Incubus ruled over weren't actually his, but in retrospect it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Also, looking back at the Demiurge's council, Mottom never actually refers to Incubus, just the fact that a &quot;prostitute&quot; was sent in his place (now we know why he didn't want to attend in person). And even Gog-Agog refers to him as a blowhard. Then again, just about anyone is going to have a hard time filling Maya's boots.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, although everyone assumed Incubus represented lust (it seemed a bit obvious at first given his name), and Gog-Agog envy due to the way she copied people, I'm suddenly wondering if it's the other way around. It's certainly looking as if his tragic flaw has more to do with envy than lust.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe the sins association is more superficial than it seems. The root of Mottom's issues were more about fear than gluttony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 02-08-2017, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"http