s://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:47:50-07:00","id":1098922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1098811#post1098811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-5-53/\" target=\"_blank\">Is the lack of comments people being wise?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they need to be approved, so it takes a while for them to show up after a new page drops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T16:32:10-07:00","id":1098938,"title":"","content":"Holy fuck how am I only finding out about this webcomic now? This is amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T08:36:04-07:00","id":1106071,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-6-58/\" target=\"_blank\">Latest page - the heist is about to begin</a><br /> <br /> All of the fan-created demons would make great custom demon to be summoned - perhaps with white-blue-red first circle, green-gold second circle and ebon third circle, or perhaps Himself is the only one that truly approaches the power of a third circle demon.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://infinitedevilengine.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The rest of the devil submissions are going up here</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","user":"doran","date":". 06-21-2017, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1794-doran","name":"doran","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T01:26:09-07:00","id":1110488,"title":"","content":"The actual comic is now catching up to the point of elaborating on the place of Mammon's people in his backstory.<br /> <br /> \u200bI find the image of him plaintively looking up while all of his fellows have their heads bowed to be strangely compelling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:21:49-07:00","id":1110639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1110488#post1110488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The actual comic is now catching up to the point of elaborating on the place of Mammon's people in his backstory.<br /> <br /> I find the image of him plaintively looking up while all of his fellows have their heads bowed to be strangely compelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is interesting that in the same panel in which their name is given as the Kind People they are called cruel. The term is usually applied to the fey as a means of avoiding offense.<br /> <br /> Also, besides buying his key, Mammon also killed his kin to protect his hoard. Perhaps they had some kind of claim to it, didn't respect his exclusive ownership, or servile and thieves are not mutually exclusive.<br /> <br /> Edit: I checked and there are Kind People serving Mammon still in the same banker robes as humans, but apparently none of them are kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 07-02-2017, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:40:09-07:00","id":1110647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1110639#post1110639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is interesting that in the same panel in which their name is given as the Kind People they are called cruel.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe lore card already noted that their name is a bit ironic, largely because they're rather martial creatures, built to protect their loads with violence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, besides buying his key, Mammon also killed his kin to protect his hoard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Cio told us that ages ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bWith this context, I'm guessing that Mammon's action was driven more by his own paranoia and a bit of resentment for how he had been treated.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">or servile and thieves are not mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt seems unlikely; they have a caste system based on the people that they serve, with the couriers for merchants placed more highly than even kings. It seems unlikely to me that orthodox Kind People care much about material possessions at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: I checked and there are Kind People serving Mammon still in the same banker robes as humans, but apparently none of them are kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI suspect that the Bank of the Grand Dragon is a haven for ambitious Kind People. Not necessarily because Mammon cares for them (he cares only for the Count, after all), but because he's a steady employer to such folk, and many of them see him as an inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T17:17:09-07:00","id":1110697,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm just wondering what the twist is.<br /> <br /> Unlike Mottom and Incubus, we've only seen Mammon through second-hand accounts, and he hasn't uttered a single line. As a result, I don't expect the reality of the Grand Dragon to be as advertised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T18:16:28-07:00","id":1110712,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit compelled by the possibility that Mammon will never speak, and remain comparatively enigmatic and strange, with whatever might come of contact with him conveyed solely through body language.<br /> <br /> \u200bGiven the idea that he's so enamoured of his hoard that he's gone for centuries at a time without leaving it, I suddenly have this image in which his final fate has the fortress just closed up, and he's left counting his coins for eternity, and he might barely notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T14:12:13-07:00","id":1115250,"title":"","content":"I can't believe I didn't know of this webcomic. It's breathtaking.<br /> <br /> Also, now I know who's the young woman Isator Levi uses as their avatar. I <i>wa