yle=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:11:25-07:00","id":1125453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>L'het'esh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1125438#post1125438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a devil. It may just want to see what she does.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about devils gives you the impression that they're like that?<br /> <br /> Gold devils are known for being cunning, treacherous and mercenary, so I would say that if any of them was going to start eliminating people from the group, a gold would be the first choice.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would speculate that her perspective is that Allison isn't really contributing any distinct skills to the operation, and if she understands Allison to be the one who commissioned it, then she might see her elimination as a prime opportunity to redirect the group towards a more profitable and less foolhardy venture than infiltrating the deepest levels of Mammon's inner sanctum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T06:30:10-07:00","id":1125575,"title":"","content":"I expect she's about to reel Allison in somehow and is just doing it this way because it's funnier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T09:07:44-07:00","id":1125611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1125453#post1125453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...\u200bI would speculate that her perspective is that Allison isn't really contributing any distinct skills to the operation, and if she understands Allison to be the one who commissioned it, then she might see her elimination as a prime opportunity to redirect the group towards a more profitable and less foolhardy venture than infiltrating the deepest levels of Mammon's inner sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>while also eliminating Oskar and the others behind Allison? That's too many 'nasty boys' that might want to, erm, <i>discuss</i> the matter later.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like my Avatar? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:35:04-07:00","id":1125636,"title":"","content":"Allison is the last in line. You'll notice that Oskar and the others are already heading into the next room when Suuz cuts the wire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T11:10:19-07:00","id":1125649,"title":"","content":"Charon was behind Allison in the prior page, although I would warrant that he could make that jump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T02:37:16-07:00","id":1125831,"title":"","content":"Also, to quote the gilded devil lore card:<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;They typically bear absolutely no sense of allegiance, friendship or empathy to any save those that serve their needs, and are perfectly willing to sacrifice their servants and retainers by the dozens to achieve some minor goal.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSo that might provide a bit of context for Suuz's actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-08T22:50:46-07:00","id":1126591,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-6-70/\" target=\"_blank\">New offering</a> Welp, Travel without Distance is always nice to have handy. Coming next - Brawl Charms!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:15:05-07:00","id":1126607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1125453#post1125453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI would speculate that her perspective is that Allison isn't really contributing any distinct skills to the operation, and if she understands Allison to be the one who commissioned it, then she might see her elimination as a prime opportunity to redirect the group towards a more profitable and less foolhardy venture than infiltrating the deepest levels of Mammon's inner sanctum.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would have thought, though, that someone would have mentioned &quot;hey, Allison has a ridiculous power, don't mess with her&quot; to them at some point, even if they didn't want to bring up the key specifically.<br /> <br /> Oh well, she's about to learn it the hard way.<br /> <br /> Although I do wonder if this is going to set off any of Mammon's alarms...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-09-2017, 03:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T00:30:52-07:00","id":1126612,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair Allison hasn't really demonstrated a lot of control with it till now. As far as most are concerned she has great potential, but no known limits and terrible odds of being able to use them helpfully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:25:23-07:00","id":1126823,"title":"","content":"I don't know, it seems to me that surprising a person with vast, uncontrolled power and dropping them suddenly into a pit with lots of aggressive shapeshifting monstrosities that will immediately attack them would be an exceedingly good way to cause some sort of explosion that would set off every alarm for miles if it didn't actually vaporize you as collateral damage. That kind of target calls for quiet assassination with plausible deniability, not an impulsive kick into a Burmese tiger trap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T14:09:48-07:00","id":1128956,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-6-71/\" target=\"_blank\">Welp, thanks for playing, Suuz</a>. Something tells me that only main characters are going to survive to the end of this run.<br /> <br /> Something interesting that occurred to me: While the Seven are clearly each associated with one obvious sin, when we get to know them better each one's problem actually seems to be a <i>different</i> sin. For instance:<br /> <br /> Mottom was presented as gluttony, but in fact she's being forced to put up that facade due to her weak position. If we had to name one for her, her real sin is probably <i>sloth</i>, although cowardice would be a better word for it - she refuses to use her power to try and change the situation.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Incubus was presented as lustful and seductive, but once we saw him in-person there wasn't any real sign of that. I'd say his real sin is <i>envy</i> - he's completely consumed by jealousy of the other demiurges. (You could argue that he's Pride instead, since it's his wounded pride that's making him lash out at them.)<br /> <br /> I wonder if that applies to the others as well? We've seen some evidence that Mammon might actually be wrath (since he killed his own kin.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-14-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T15:48:41-07:00","id":1128995,"title":"","content":"...I wonder of if the Beast of God will be undone by pride.","signature":"<hr class