r? Courtesy of<span style=\"color:#0000FF\"> Jen</span>! : <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Anybody want their characters to be experimented on ? </span>post 98<br /> <i>An Exalt is never unarmed.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4018-l-het-esh","name":"L'het'esh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T21:22:20-07:00","id":1152706,"title":"","content":"Actually, that sum comes up several times in that book. 30 pieces of silver is also what the sons os Jacob got for selling their brother. It's also the fine recomended in Deutsronomy a rapist must pay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T23:30:59-07:00","id":1152725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>L'het'esh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1152695#post1152695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why say silver? Why not gold? Why link this to the 30 pieces supposedly paid a traitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>My best guess is resonance of some kind. It's not that the Bible's story inspired Mammon, it's more like the legendary betrayal of Mammon kept resonating in the multiverse, taking millions of forms in different places.<br /> In the same way that King Zoss isn't &quot;our&quot; Zeus - he's the actual legend whose resonance coalesced in Zeus' story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3657-sagara","name":"Sagara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3657_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T09:24:58-07:00","id":1152828,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-7-87/\" target=\"_blank\">New Offering </a><br /> <br /> Silver For Betrayal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T05:24:21-08:00","id":1163517,"title":"","content":"Multiple new offerings since the last post, but<br /> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/seeker-of-thrones-8-96/\" target=\"_blank\">here's the newest</a>:<br /> <br /> A few significant character design changes over the last several pages: Cio's horns, a new white chunk in Allison's hair, and now...well, the alt text sums it up as &quot;Princess Jack Moonshine.&quot; I'm kind of wondering what, if anything, provoked that, but hopefully we'll find out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:25:26-08:00","id":1164085,"title":"","content":"Indignation and the fear of death, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:01:22-08:00","id":1164089,"title":"","content":"Good for him.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's possible that Abbadon is just having a bit of a joke there, and the red devil's name is something entirely different to what Allison bound the blue devil with. The exact terms of names and devil binding... they've been elucidated upon, but not depicted directly in a way that would make it clear how they work and what it means for a devil to shed names. Complicated a bit more when we're told that sometimes they have names that aren't even <i>really</i> their names, so to speak; the ebon devil that Cio used to be is supposed to have had a name that was long and twisty and possibly impronouncable, with Yabalchoath apparently being somewhere between a snippet and a vague approximation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere's also been references in the lore cards to the idea of devils figuring out names inside of the names that they're bound with, and that this is something to be wary of. I think it was most overt in the pale devil card, with the idea that their low intelligence makes them singularly unsuited to contemplation of their binding names and discerning other names from within them.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo with Princess, I'd say it's a matter of having once known a true name that belonged to itself giving her a better insight into seeing through the bindings than most, and having presumably gone through all or most of the previous forms in the distant past, the combination of desperation with a sense of the violent situation being familiar was sufficient to let her recall a red devil's name from amidst all of the dross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:20:09-08:00","id":1164092,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, the more I wonder if the pact Allison made with Vladok has anything to do with it. She got a Devil's Kiss placed on her, which may still connect her to the black flame that Vladok was and Princess is now. Since Allison has Incubus in turn hooked up to her, this may be feeding into it.<br /> <br /> Probably not, but it's a thought.<br /> <br /> Also, someone pointed out a nice bit of parallel:<br /> <br /> Here: &quot;Nae! Nae! I'll not end this way!&quot;<br /> <br /> Before: &quot;<a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/wielder-of-names-2-30/\" target=\"_blank\">Nay! Nay! You shalt no