of royalty now that we know Mammon is Tower, but Prim's story below really drove it home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>But sexually.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1797-ellis","name":"Ellis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1797_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:12:59-08:00","id":1181001,"title":"","content":"We're one page into him actually interacting with Alice and he's already become the most sympathetic demiurge.<br /> <br /> The Prim story was <i>extremely</i> strong in this context as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:58:09-08:00","id":1181012,"title":"","content":"So it looks like he's not dead (the way I speculated earlier), but it <i>is</i> likely true that pretty much everything is now handled for him by his bureaucracy. It's also amusing that Cio interpreted his behind-the-scenes financial manipulations against her as some sort of clever scheme on his part, when it was probably just his panicked priests doing what they could to undermine her while knowing that they couldn't rely on Mammon himself.<br /> <br /> (It's still a bit <i>suspicious</i> that Cio can't remember what happened in there past a certain point, which makes it possible that she might not even have stolen a key after all - it's entirely possible he actually gave it to her for one reason or another, if he's in this state all the time.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T23:05:38-08:00","id":1181027,"title":"","content":"He seems like such a nice old dragon. I wanna give him a grandad sweater and a pipe and a cup of tea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T01:13:54-08:00","id":1181042,"title":"","content":"See, I don't think that Mammon is senile by virtue of having literally forgotten what value his treasure ever held for him. I think that at some point, he experienced an existential crisis at the point where he had gathered so much that he didn't even know everything he had and stopped to think &quot;what even is the point of all this&quot;, and failed along his path to Royalty by doubling down and saying &quot;surely if I just take inventory on it all, I'll rediscover whatever passion or purpose I had in collecting it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T09:59:24-08:00","id":1181156,"title":"","content":"I do wonder if this isn't something like his default state. His people were called the kindly ones, and if they could be right arses, they didn't appear threatening enough to deserve that euphemism given all the other things around that might take offense.<br /> <br /> Perhaps all the skulls of his family weren't trophies or warnings, but an attempt to be nice to what remained of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T11:38:11-08:00","id":1181177,"title":"","content":"I don't think that they are entirely called the Kind People in jest; their culture is focused on the virtues of service to others, as they were created to be couriers and messengers of the gods. There's a measure of irony to it because they can be fierce combatants, but that is still focused in service. It matters so much to them that they're ranked in a caste system based on who one serves (the servers of merchants rank highest).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T01:06:55-08:00","id":1181938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1181042#post1181042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't think that Mammon is senile by virtue of having literally forgotten what value his treasure ever held for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's looking more and more like he's a doddering old beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T02:01:30-08:00","id":1181944,"title":"","content":"man, I never thought I'd feel bad for the Immortal god king of ten thousand realities on an infinite spire of gold, brimming with power and heir to a fragment of the universal creator, but here we are.<br /> <br /> I wonder what part he played in the hunting of Zoss, if any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T08:58:25-08:00","id":1182005,"title":"","content":"Seeing Mammon like that has caused me to revise some of my presumptions about the nature of the Bank of the Grand Dragon, and the worlds that it presides over. After all, it occurred to me that we know precious little of Mammon's domain, compared to several of the others.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's probably still not especially good, but it might be less severely exploitative than I had supposed.<br /> <br /> \u200bMammon has also been referred to as the least powerful of the Seven, and on top of his physical capabilities, it may be that his functional empire is the smallest and does not expand (keeping in mind that, while each of them nominally has authority over 111,111 universes, many of those have not yet had their gates opened or been subjugated).<br /> <br /> \u200bBefore, I had wondered if the Bank might have been something that was developed out of his need to have assistance in counting his hoard. Now I'm wondering if it might actually be something that evolved out of all the people who journeyed to rob or slay him, and between the inability to do so, how pitiful he was, and a possible difficulty in getting out again, stayed behind, their descendants becoming a society of his devotees.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-03T13:54:56-08:00","id":1182060,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's possible that the bank was originally a financial empire that increased the hoard by reaping a portion of the conquests of the other demiurges. It was mentioned that Mottom was taking out loans to fund her lavish court. After he started slipping into apathy it might have continued out of inertia though lacked his presiding will. Or perhaps it grew so large that he was no longer able to manage it personally and that was part of what led to his disengagement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":