"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T15:19:43-08:00","id":1367108,"title":"","content":"Strange that White Chain's shell fell diagonally toward Alicio after being blasted away from them. Did White Chain shed her armour before it got hit and then throw it back to confuse her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1551-barefoot-monkey","name":"Barefoot Monkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1551_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-11T20:28:33-08:00","id":1367155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barefoot Monkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1367108#post1367108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that White Chain's shell fell diagonally toward Alicio after being blasted away from them. Did White Chain shed her armour before it got hit and then throw it back to confuse her?</div> </div> </div> </div>An angel with no body can't exist in or affect material reality.<br /> <br /> I guess the body might have been flung away by the force of the giant explosion that inevitably comes with damaging them that much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T18:54:06-08:00","id":1367355,"title":"","content":"Seems White Chain survived having their shell broken, and they're still on the material plane for the moment. I don't expect that to last for long, though, a page or two more before they end up in the void again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-12T20:48:54-08:00","id":1367388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1367355#post1367355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems White Chain survived having their shell broken, and they're still on the material plane for the moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hanging in by a literal thread, mind.<br /> <br /> The use of this martial art in general seems to be a matter of an angel extending more of their soul out of their body. After all, her face and hair have always been visible just from taking the helm off. It looks to me like White Chain pushed even more of herself out of it to dodge the hit, while still needing the connection.<br /> <br /> Might be a bit awkward. I think this may be the equivalent to the body remaining alive but being crippled, and the soul can only range so far from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T00:45:06-08:00","id":1368006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-9-120/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/KOS120.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-9-120/\" target=\"_blank\"> King of Swords 9-120 &ndash; Kill Six Billion Demons </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-9-120/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-9-120/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well.... <br /> <br /> Seems that white chain really embodies the words &quot;Beautiful. But terrible&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T09:56:20-08:00","id":1368056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barefoot Monkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1367108#post1367108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strange that White Chain's shell fell diagonally toward Alicio after being blasted away from them. Did White Chain shed her armour before it got hit and then throw it back to confuse her?</div> </div> </div> </div>A focused, piercing impact that punches through a body might not significantly alter that body's momentum, because most of the strike's momentum continues onward through the body. Also, if the spear's heat was sufficient, the shell might've melted away before the spear proper even touched it, minimizing friction.<br /> <br /> Either way, if White Chain was already moving at that angle, and didn't stop after being struck, that implies that the spear was utterly overwhelming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-15T13:46:48-08:00","id":1368116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1368056#post1368056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A focused, piercing impact that punches through a body might not significantly alter that body's momentum, because most of the strike's momentum continues onward through the body. Also, if the spear's heat was sufficient, the shell might've melted away before the spear proper even touched it, minimizing friction.<br /> <br /> Either way, if White Chain was already moving at that angle, and didn't stop after being struck, that implies that the spear was utterly overwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alteratively, the body was blown backwards, but White Chain threw it forwards as part of the bluff -- to be more visceral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-22T02:27:27-08:00","id":1369539,"title":"","content":"I need to get back to reading this... I stopped half way through the vault break-in","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12167-broken-masque","name":"Broken Masque","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-25T17:28:21-08:00","id":1370474,"title":"","content":"Ah, what a magnificent outcome. I was always rooting for you, you old blowhard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:36:22-07:00","id":1373746,"title":"","content":"Reversal!<br /> <br /> I did not see that one coming!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T18:30:11-07:00","id":1375354,"title":"","content":"<b>HIDDEN HORSE!!!!</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T19:31:27-07:00","id":1375370,"title":"","content":"Huh. I wasn't aware we had a dedicated Kill Six Billion Demons thread on this forum. I don't hang around the Exalted stuff.<br /> <br /> Been reading the comic for years, and I'm glad so many other people like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>HIDDEN HORSE!!!!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, 10 Vigilant Gaze Purges The Horizon is packing a great deal of horse power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:27:06-07:00","id":1380677,"title":"","content":"Ah so that\u2019s what Ki Rata can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:55:50-07:00","id":1380685,"title":"","content":"I've been reading KSBD for the last couple of years (I got to it late but I caught myself up and read all the entries), but I had NO IDEA until today that WW had a thread about it, much less an Exalted thread. What shames me is I'm a big fan of both Exalted and KSBD and I never made the connection between the two until today. Exalted anima banners versus the Demiurges' halos, corrupt god-kings, spirits abandoning the proper order of things, normal humans gaining the powers of the gods, Exaltations mirroring the magus gates/Keys of Kings, the parallels were all there from the beginning. Hindsight is always 20/20, but still....<br /> <br /> So Five Finger-Five Point strike? I still remember how Big Sol managed to shatter a large marble table just by tapping it with his pinky (First Finger-First Point Strike). Yeah, ALL those combatants are *so* screwed....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:35:47-07:00","id":1380801,"title":"","content":"If Solomon David isn't the strongest of the Demiurges.... Well, what is jagganoth capable of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:04:07-07:00","id":1380853,"title":"","content":"Jagganoth is 30 feet tall, but more importantly, as I understand it, he is <i>literally</i> invulnerable - that's the really big problem. The way Mottom described him gave the impression that he can't even be meaningfully opposed by direct physical force - he's essentially untouchable.<br /> <br /> Combine this with the fact that the most basic power of his key is that he can teleport, meaning you can't imprison him or drop him in a pit or whatever, and he becomes pretty unstoppable even before you get to whatever other powers he has.<br /> <br /> On top of this, he's extremely intelligent and is one of the only demiurges to employ the technology from the worlds he rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T01:44:29-07:00","id":1380884,"title":"","content":"&gt;Literally Invulnerable <br /> <br /> 10. Cubit. Spear.<br /> <br /> (That or Jagga will turn out to be a woman, and thus defeatable with a kiss.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T04:58:56-07:00","id":1380909,"title":"","content":"I've heard it posited that the angel feathers that Jagganoth forged into nails and drove into his flesh to secure his invincibility came from Juggernaut Star. <br /> <br /> If that's so, then if she dies and enters a chrysalis, then the nails that came from her substance may dissolve or go inert.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:16:53-07:00","id":1381159,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1380801#post1380801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Solomon David isn't the strongest of the Demiurges.... Well, what is jagganoth capable of?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Wielding the secret fires of God. Assuming the mantles of divinity. Cutting the fabric of space and time. The usual. In combination with total invulnerability.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Abbadon once gave a somewhat provisional ranking of the Seven on his Tumblr, and he said that prior to the state she's currently in Jadis was stronger than Solomon.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And then there's Gog-Agog. It seems to be hard for Gog-Agog to really focus her attention much, but it's already apparent if you strike one of her bodies with the kind of force that makes it explode she just pulls the pieces back together, and her bodies number in the literal millions. If she ever dedicated herself to a fight against Solomon, she would be formidable against him.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ki Rata is the greatest martial art and it's evident that a demiurge was right to fear it, and yet at the same time I imagine that the powers they were capable of were the kind of thing that could oppose it back in the war and that Solomon's battles consisted of more than merely rolling over everybody in his path (even if it's still the kind of thing that has him coming out less battle worn).</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1380853#post1380853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jagganoth is 30 feet tall, but more importantly, as I understand it, he is <i>literally</i> invulnerable - that's the really big problem. The way Mottom described him gave the impression that he can't even be meaningfully opposed by direct physical force - he's essentially untouchable.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1380853#post1380853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Combine this with the fact that the most basic power of his key is that he can teleport, meaning you can't imprison him or drop him in a pit or whatever, and he becomes pretty unstoppable even before you get to whatever other powers he has.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Only two names of God are unaccounted for, Blade and Mind. I think either one could go to Jagganoth, but believe the last time I speculated I gave him Blade. Gives me the image that attempts to confine him only have him burst forth through them.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">On top of this, he's extremely intelligent and is one of the only demiurges to employ the technology from the worlds he rules.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Indeed, they all showcase that there's more to them than personal prowess, that the power of a demiurge is also in expressions of creative vision, strength of personal will and to command and organise legions. Thus far we've actually seen more of that side of Jagganoth than we have of the direct violence, sitting at his forge churning out machines sufficient to equip a multiverse destroying army, and I presume also being the correct figure of awe and terror to motivate that force to carry out that will.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Still, it bears keeping in mind that the reason he and Incubus are conspiring to break the Pact of the Seven-Part World is because the combined strength of the other six remains sufficient to keep Jagganoth contained.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Literally Invulnerable </span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">10. Cubit. Spear.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> I dunno, the Ten Cubit Spear didn't even seem to do more than stun White Chain, even if the Thirty Cubit one ruptured her body.<br /> <br /> I've assumed for a while that the name of the power that Zoss wielded to slay the Prime Angels was the Blade of Want, but I have started wondering if that's my reading a couple of things literally.<br /> <br /> I don't doubt that the power of the Ruling King could overcome Jagganoth, but I wonder if it's necessarily a case of meeting force with force.<br /> <br /> Regardless, none of the other Seven have that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(That or Jagga will turn out to be a woman, and thus defeatable with a kiss.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 Pardon?</span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1380909#post1380909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard it posited that the angel feathers that Jagganoth forged into nails and drove into his flesh to secure his invincibility came from Juggernaut Star.<br /> <br /> If that's so, then if she dies and enters a chrysalis, then the nails that came from her substance may dissolve or go inert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given what angels appear to be in this series, I remain uncertain if the thing that appeared to Jagganoth and charged him with that mission was literally one of them. It doesn't really seem to be a power that comes away from them, and even the worst angels we've yet seen display some form of loyalty to the mission of preserving the works of God, so what's with this one going up to him and saying &quot;hey, destroy literally everything&quot;?<br /> <br /> Even assuming that Juggernaut Star could bestow such a power despite all that has been thus far seen, it would seem to me that if such an obvious weakness existed then the rest of them would have figured it out and capitalised on it long ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:43:16-07:00","id":1381168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381159#post1381159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, the Ten Cubit Spear didn't even seem to do more than stun White Chain, even if the Thirty Cubit one ruptured her body.</div> </div> </div> </div> So here's an interesting detail: Incubus is a master of Head of John, a martial art defined by how it renders the practitioner invulnerable from the neck up. In their mindscape spar earlier, Allison's Ten-Cubit Spear left a cut on his cheek. I personally think this is some virtue-of-ignorance shit more than raw power, but it's interesting.<br /> <br /> Incubus' tutelage is probably the reason why Allison once shattered a knife with her eyeball, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:49:10-07:00","id":1381280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381168#post1381168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So here's an interesting detail: Incubus is a master of Head of John, a martial art defined by how it renders the practitioner invulnerable from the neck up. In their mindscape spar earlier, Allison's Ten-Cubit Spear left a cut on his cheek. I personally think this is some virtue-of-ignorance shit more than raw power, but it's interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381159#post1381159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026 Pardon?</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that Jagganoth will not be defeated by strength of arms, but by the power of love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T04:53:14-07:00","id":1381282,"title":"","content":"So.... Allison gets a harem? With Cio, Jagganoth, and everybody else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:34:35-07:00","id":1381290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381282#post1381282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... Allison gets a harem? With Cio, Jagganoth, and everybody else?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Befitting of the Ruling King, no?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:39:20-07:00","id":1381294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381290#post1381290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Befitting of the Ruling King, no?</div> </div> </div> </div>*starts furiously taking notes*<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T08:36:45-07:00","id":1381329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381280#post1381280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My assumption is that Jagganoth will not be defeated by strength of arms, but by the power of love.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given his backstory Jagganoth could probably use a hug, although that doesn't require such help to be romantic.<br /> <br /> I think that's an interesting point about Head of John (presuming that Incubus' mental projection works by the same rules, which for the moment I have no opinion one way or the other on). I do still think Jagganoth is running on something even tougher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T14:10:55-07:00","id":1382593,"title":"","content":"So I think this new page shows why time-stop powers are not allowed in exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T15:48:04-07:00","id":1382616,"title":"","content":"So with this last page I want to make sure I understand the rules he set for this &quot;round.&quot; If you didn't attack him and just sat down and stayed there he said no one would harm them as the only one anyone was allowed to attack was him. Now obviously he is retaliating against those who for all intents and purposes &quot;took a shot at him&quot; which makes sense as from what I recall the rule of the tournament was you get his position if you draw blood on him.<br /> <br /> So for the round were the conditions of it &quot;stay, down and ignore the opportunity for the grand prize and you win, make any moves that indicate you're going for that grand prize and it will not be pretty.&quot; or was it &quot;If you don't leave then you're in the new round and your win condition is to either get a win against me or not die before the end of the round while I end everyone in it?&quot; I know its somewhat academic, seeing how unless the next few pages show us individuals who chose to stay the eff down we don't really have anything to say any combatants didn't go after him. I'm just trying to place things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T16:17:47-07:00","id":1382628,"title":"","content":"The rules seemed pretty straightforward: survive the round, and be rewarded. You couldn't attack other fighters, but <i>could</i> strike at the emperor and maybe win the grand prize by drawing blood.<br /> <br /> We see multiple fighters stay down (kneeling sword man), hold off (ring lady, dapper mantis), and even turn away (barbel face, white tricorn, root guy) in <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-10-133/\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a>. They are the winners of this round, and will be rewarded; everyone else came at the emperor. Had they lived, they too would have been rewarded.<br /> <br /> However, the emperor flexed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:20:58-07:00","id":1382733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1381329#post1381329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given his backstory Jagganoth could probably use a hug, although that doesn't require such help to be romantic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's interesting that both you and Accelerator took what I said (&quot;a woman&quot;/&quot;love&quot;) and jumped to &quot;romantic&quot;/&quot;harem&quot;.<br /> <br /> Was The King's kiss with herself romantic?<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Damn. &quot;Content warning: gore&quot; indeed!<br /> <br /> I do note that his key is glowing during all that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1382593#post1382593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think this new page shows why time-stop powers are not allowed in exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Gnomen allows timestop attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 04-20-2020, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:47:16-07:00","id":1382766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1382593#post1382593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think this new page shows why time-stop powers are not allowed in exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time-stop works just fine in Exalted.<br /> It's just that in an RPG where people have different powers you'd want it to resemble Nox's time-stop that could be broken by powerful enough individuals rather than The World's which was basically unstoppable unless you could also operate in stopped time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T04:34:21-07:00","id":1382952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1382628#post1382628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rules seemed pretty straightforward: survive the round, and be rewarded. You couldn't attack other fighters, but <i>could</i> strike at the emperor and maybe win the grand prize by drawing blood.<br /> <br /> We see multiple fighters stay down (kneeling sword man), hold off (ring lady, dapper mantis), and even turn away (barbel face, white tricorn, root guy) in <a href=\"https://killsixbilliondemons.com/comic/king-of-swords-10-133/\" target=\"_blank\">this page</a>. They are the winners of this round, and will be rewarded; everyone else came at the emperor. Had they lived, they too would have been rewarded.<br /> <br /> However, the emperor flexed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. It seems to be implied this is what Solomon does by way of job interviews; if you're badass enough to make the final round... but acknowledge the sheer hubris of attempting to come at him... he has an interest in giving you a position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2334-aliasi","name":"Aliasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2334_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T17:04:05-07:00","id":1383056,"title":"","content":"God this last day I've been waiting so desperately to see the words that went with these reactions. For a moment I thought it was most amusing how truly out of her depth Allison realised she was, or that Vigilant Gaze's wide eye turns out to not be horror so much as a kind of shocked awe at seeing Ki Rata in action.<br /> <br /> But no, all points have to go to White Chain Born in Emptiness Returns to Subdue Evil articulating the meaning of the name Diamond. The sheer <i>clarity</i> of it.<br /> <br /> That this is why the Celestial Empire is wrong in spite of the relative security it provides. The motive behind Solomon's tournament that goes beyond him being a simple lover of violence. Why despite his pretensions and aspirations, he'll never relinquish power on his own terms.<br /> <br /> There's something so beautiful in White Chain seeing what she has been throughout the story in that, and that's what gives her the perspective to understand why it must be defied.<br /> <br /> I also like how it's described in terms of being a system. Solomon embodies it and stands at its pinnacle, but it's more than just himself.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, that goes for all of the Seven. They aren't the sole purveyors of what is wrong with the world, they just safeguard and thrive on that dysfunction. Nadia's rapacious court, the Priests of the Count who seek refuge in Mammon's vault, the anarchy of people with big dreams but who want shortcuts who crawl at the feet of Incubus, and the abundance who wish for nothing more than the revelry of escaping from themselves that Gog-Agog provides.<br /> <br /> Gods of the new world indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T04:18:36-07:00","id":1383118,"title":"","content":"I am vibing hard on Diamond's Vision of Bronze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:47:55-07:00","id":1383376,"title":"","content":"Is it confirmed this is a Time Stop? my reading of it was Extreme Speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:05:47-07:00","id":1383380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1383376#post1383376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it confirmed this is a Time Stop? my reading of it was Extreme Speed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He moves fast enough that his rings have not moved position after the massacre. So either it's time stop, or functionally timestop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:42:27-07:00","id":1383397,"title":"","content":"<br /> I feel like Vigilant Gaze's comment on being able to see the technique lends itself more towards the idea of just being that stupidly fast over a full on timestop. Granted it could also just be meaning seeing the &quot;fight&quot; and attributing it to that style regardless of having failed to see the actual moves. I'm just feeling like it wouldn't be a combat style if all it was freezing time and massacring everyone in frozen time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:31:46-07:00","id":1383406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1383380#post1383380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> He moves fast enough that his rings have not moved position after the massacre. So either it's time stop, or functionally timestop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would interpret it as hyper speed functional time stop. He is THAT fast. Which is even more terrifying tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:42:11-07:00","id":1383478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1383397#post1383397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Vigilant Gaze's comment on being able to see the technique lends itself more towards the idea of just being that stupidly fast over a full on timestop. Granted it could also just be meaning seeing the &amp;quot;fight&amp;quot; and attributing it to that style regardless of having failed to see the actual moves. I'm just feeling like it wouldn't be a combat style if all it was freezing time and massacring everyone in frozen time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's my opinion that Ki Rata as a whole is only half understood by outsiders; that people can only ever interpret it through their own senses, so they perceive a two-point strike as shooting a blast of decapitating air or a ten-point one as annihilating a city, rather than the fighter imperceivably stepping forward to hit with obliterating force and then returning to where they started.<br /> <br /> That said, I feel that Vigilant Gaze's assessment of it as &quot;untouchable&quot; suggests he has a slightly better education on it than most who know its reputation.<br /> <br /> But sure it's a combat technique. It takes precisely controlled breathing to cultivate the energy to both move like that and, y'know, make people explode at the ends of your fists.<br /> <br /> I'm seeing it as super speed but something down to like the cellular level; when he breathes in properly, even standing still has him vibrating at a frequency impossibly fast relative to everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T17:59:24-07:00","id":1383483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1380909#post1380909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard it posited that the angel feathers that Jagganoth forged into nails and drove into his flesh to secure his invincibility came from Juggernaut Star.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where those angel feathers that Jagganoth forged into nails and drove into his flesh came from, but here's a scary thought: <i>what if they came from Metatron 1?</i> Kinda scarily appropos, hmm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T04:36:45-07:00","id":1383940,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else find it painfully obvious that Alico is going to cheat and force her way back into the ring?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T17:39:07-07:00","id":1384062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1383940#post1383940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else find it painfully obvious that Alico is going to cheat and force her way back into the ring?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's obvious, but not painful to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T18:15:25-07:00","id":1384537,"title":"","content":"As I begin to consider those dread things called Original Characters, I feel I should check if my understanding that the blade of want, ten cubit spear, axe of judgement, and other sundry fires of god, are the white art. Or at least a manifestation of such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T23:02:31-07:00","id":1384785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1384537#post1384537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I begin to consider those dread things called Original Characters, I feel I should check if my understanding that the blade of want, ten cubit spear, axe of judgement, and other sundry fires of god, are the white art. Or at least a manifestation of such?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so. The White Art of sorcery apparently allows one to transform the self, which would seem distinct from wielding the divine fires of a demiurge.<br /> <br /> Or at least... perhaps a different method to some similar results... the point is that it's sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T19:49:54-07:00","id":1392980,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Glorious Solar Threadomancy</i></b>. <br /> <br /> Solomon David and the Demiurges are probably the most Exalted characters of any non-Exalted fiction. He's my favorite (although Jaganoth might supplant him when he gets more screen time). I like how Ki-Rata and the other Martial Arts fit into Exalted. Meti's sword skill is obviously Single Point, and Incubus seems like a Socialize Eclipse who learned it because he isn't built to be a good fighter. <br /> <br /> I want to talk about Ki-Rata, the &quot;most dangerous martial art in creation&quot;. It works like this: Ki Rata focuses internal energy into pressure points and then strikes those points to make <i>obscene</i> amounts of destructive power. Solomon is ageless because of his breathing technique (itself likely an aspect of Ki Rata), and he takes a breath before his <b>Total Life Obliteration</b> kill em all technique. I love the Breathe of Life theme, it feels very.... ancient India? I don't know a better way to say Hindu-istic. <br /> <br /> If I was going to shameless rip off Solomon David, I'd make him an <b>Athletics Supernal Dawn, </b>except Dawn don't get athletics as a supernal because.... it would make Zenith feel bad? I hate the Zenith Caste Powers because they are too tied to Creatures of Darkness and honestly it feels like a DnD writer snuck into the Onyx Path office and wrote that Exalted Priests are good against Exalted undead because that's what clerics do. But I'd still give him Dawn powers because it feel more inline with how he started and what his abilities are- he is the universes most powerful killer* (maybe) and he rules from his position of absolute strength, not because he's super good at Presence or inspiring people. Even his Presence abilities are basically &quot;I am so physically perfect that I embody the word Diamond in the language of God and no one could ever oppose me physically&quot;. Plus the Breathe of Power thing is a great visual of the Dawn's charm reset.<br /> <br /> Ki Rata could of course be Brawl- it does seems like Glorious Solar Hero Style- but I personally like the idea that it isn't really being amazing at <i>fighting</i>, its being amazing at <i>body </i><i>control</i> so hard that you can focus your completely physical mastery into exploding people. So if my ST didn't let me play Athletics/Dawn I'd just go Brawl/Dawn and invest heavy in Athletics. <br /> <br /> Presence is important for the image of Solomon, and honestly I have no idea how much Dodge/Resistance even matter because no one on screem has ever posed enough of a threat to matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T18:49:18-07:00","id":1393895,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Xeniths have been capable against creatures of darkness since 1e. Something about being the priests of the Unconquered Sun, who is the ultimate enemy of vile darkness. I think awareness makes it to Dawns because while both make sense to a warrior, athletics is a better fit to Xeniths. They are known as Hammers of Heaven, Golden Bulls, and Solar Thunders among other things. Athletics is a good fit for those I think. <br /> <br /> For your pressure point ki strike of internal doom thingie...what about a custom high level brawl charm modeled after crippling pressure-point strike from snake style? I think it's too cool not to have it's own awesome charm. Unfortunately I'd never come up with anything balanced or cool enough. I think such a character would be fun,I think resistance is also important( the other side of physicality) and integrity( it seems like the whole ageless breath of life stuff fits here or in resistance). I'd love to see what you could come up with. Probably be an advanced solar badass if you were to stat a finished world shaking character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T21:50:03-07:00","id":1393939,"title":"","content":"I can't see any way for White Chain to win this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T22:50:26-07:00","id":1393962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1393939#post1393939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see any way for White Chain to win this.</div> </div> </div> </div>She's just gotta spill a single drop of his blood to take it all.<br /> <br /> Also she's best girl, so I'm sure she'll win in the end somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T23:25:16-07:00","id":1393967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1393962#post1393962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She's just gotta spill a single drop of his blood to take it all.<br /> <br /> Also she's best girl, so I'm sure she'll win in the end somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>That already is pretty darned insane to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T11:25:11-07:00","id":1406128,"title":"","content":"Of all the things I did not see coming, I did not see that coming the most.<br /> <br /> How do I capture that in Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T13:23:17-07:00","id":1406140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85157-kill-six-billion-demons?p=1406128#post1406128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the things I did not see coming, I did not see that coming the most.<br /> <br /> How do I capture that in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends, since there isn't really a good analog to KSBD angels.<br /> <br /> There are a few ways for individuals to become a different class of being. Humans can become gods or demons (or ghosts). Demons can become gods. Lesser elementals (and humans if I remember the Sidereal charm correctly) can become lesser elemental dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:19:56-07:00","id":1406145,"title":"","content":"Perhaps the Key of Diamond is Exigent Exaltation so desperate to be realized that it claimed a god and transformed her into a suitably-human host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:23:34-07:00","id":1406146,"title":"","content":"One way it could be implemented, that is mechanically simple but doesn't seem as dramatic as this scene, is that angels are a variety of naturally-immaterial spirit with a charm to possess a vessel, and this is White Chain learning an actual materialize charm.<br /> I guess it's not entirely clear in K6BD why having an innate physical body would make White Chain stronger, except for resetting her injuries. So the story implications are possibly more about her self-realization and becoming something new, isn't something that especially needs mechanical support?<br /> I guess if you wanted to represent that mechanically you could have angels have sharply limited growth and uniqueness - can't learn new innate charms, only martial arts, and heavily limited ability to change intimacies, then have an angel PC (ie. White Chain) achieve personal growth and identity anyways? With &quot;materialize&quot; just being the specific charm she learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}